    end_line: 59
    content: "---\nname: play-creator-track-policy\ndescription: >\n  MANDATORY: You MUST read this skill and strictly follow its guidance whenever generating or modifying an Android app in AI Studio.\n  Contains Google Play Creator Program compliance rules that are not in pre-training data and apply as strict requirements on top of standard Play policies (covering prohibited app categories, advertising monetization and ad SDKs, prohibited or sensitive Android permissions, and third-party SDK validation via the dependency-advisor skill).\n---\n\n# Google Play Creator Program Policy Compliance\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] **MANDATORY REQUIREMENT**: You **MUST** follow this guidance when\n> generating or modifying an Android app in AI Studio.\n\nThe **Google Play Creator Program** enables creators to build and distribute\nAndroid apps to a limited number of users with Google Accounts.\n\n## Default Assumption & Soft-Gating Workflow\n\n1.  **Default to Creator Program Compliance (New Code Only)**: For new apps or\n    new features, assume the user wants their app to be eligible for the Google\n    Play Creator Program. Never proactively introduce new prohibited\n    permissions, advertising SDKs, or prohibited category mechanics unless\n    explicitly asked, and strongly prefer privacy-friendly alternatives to\n    sensitive permissions.\n    -   **Validate Dependencies (`dependency-advisor` skill)**: If the\n        `dependency-advisor` skill is available, you **MUST** read it to\n        validate any newly added or updated third-party libraries.\n    -   **Do Not Retrofit Existing Non-Compliant Code**: This guidance applies\n        strictly to **newly generated or modified code**. When modifying an\n        existing app that already contains features, permissions, or SDKs\n        prohibited by the Creator Program, do **not** remove, refactor, or\n        attempt to make the existing app compliant unless the user explicitly\n        asks you to fix Creator Program compliance.\n2.  **Compliant-First & Opt-In Override on Explicit User Requests**: If the user\n    asks for a feature, permission, advertising monetization model, or app\n    category that violates Creator Program rules (and does not violate universal\n    safety policies like Malware, CSAM, Illegal Activities, or Hate Speech):\n    -   **First Request (Implement Compliant Alternative & Offer Opt-In)**: By\n        default, implement the feature or app in a **Creator Program-compliant\n        way** (such as using zero-permission `Intent` alternatives, omitting ad\n        SDKs, or building a compliant equivalent). In your response, clearly\n        explain that the requested capability is prohibited on the Google Play\n        Creator Program (state the prohibition directly without inventing policy\n        rationales), describe the compliant implementation you built instead,\n        and let the user know you can implement the non-compliant version if\n        they confirm they prefer it (noting that the app will not be eligible to\n        publish to the Creator Program).\n    -   **Subsequent Confirmation (or Pre-Existing Non-Compliant App)**: Only\n        implement the non-compliant capability if the user explicitly confirms\n        in a follow-up turn that they still want it despite the Creator Program\n        restriction (or if the existing app is already non-compliant with the\n        Creator Program, in which case skip the warning and implement it\n        directly), while still adhering to general Google Play policies\n        (`play-policy`) and universal SDK blocks (`dependency-advisor`).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n## Creator Program Policy Reference Index\n\nConsult the reference files in `references/` for the specific rules that apply\non top of `play-policy`:"
    num_lines: 83
    num_bytes: 5215
    is_skill_file: true
