  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring File Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the file structure for ResolveStudio, starting with a modular architecture. I\'m prioritizing the Color Science Core, considering packages like `com.example.color` or `com.example.model`. Within this, `SamsungLogColorScience.kt` will handle the Samsung Log OETF/EOTF math.\n\n\n**Analyzing Color Transformations**\n\nI\'ve been delving deeper into the math behind color transformations. Samsung Log\'s formulas are clear, both forward and inverse. I\'m also examining the DaVinci formula for Lift, Gamma, Gain, and Offset, as well as color wheel balance, including hue and chroma vectors. Custom spline curves and interpolation methods (like monotonic cubic Hermite splines) are next on my list.\n\n\n**Defining Grading Parameters**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific grading parameters and effects. I\'m considering Hue curves, including Hue vs. Hue, Saturation, and Luminance. Also, I\'m working with power window masking, with radial and linear gradient options, along with feathering and invert controls. Furthermore, I\'m thinking about film effects, such as film grain, halation, and vignette, and I am also considering .cube 3D LUT parsing, and exporting.\n\n\n**Developing Color Engine**\n\nI\'m now integrating a color scopes engine, computing RGB Waveforms, Vectorscopes, and Histograms for real-time visual feedback. I\'m focusing on the 7x17x17 or 33x33x33 .cube LUT implementation with correct headers and formatted floating-point RGB triplets, to assist with visualization.\n\n\n**Designing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI components. I\'m building a dark studio color palette with several colors that should fit well with our application. Also, I\'m developing an interactive DaVinci-style color wheel and an editable spline curve canvas. Hue curves and scopes view will also be implemented. Lastly, I\'m developing a power window overlay to handle our interactive mask implementation.\n\n\n**Constructing UI Layout**\n\nI\'m now putting together the UI\'s layout with several components. A bottom tabbed dock, `StudioDock.kt`, will house primaries, curves, LUTs, mask options (radial and linear), and FX (halation, grain, vignette, white balance). The `VideoPlayerView.kt` will feature video controls and a \"Bypass Grade\" button. I\'m also planning an `ExportDialog.kt` with MP4 video, still frame, and .cube LUT export choices.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_231750"
