dicated layout container has been built for the UI Studio Dock (`app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/StudioDockContainer.kt`), organizing the color grading tools and real-time broadcast scopes:\n\n#### Architecture & Features:\n1. **Unified Dock Header Bar**:\n   - Status badge and active tool indicator (Primary Wheels, Custom Splines, 3D LUTs, Power Window, Film FX).\n   - **Monitor Layout Selector**:\n     - **`Scope + Tool` (Split Mode)**: Simultaneously displays the live broadcast scope monitor directly above the active grading controls so you can watch your signal respond in real-time as you drag color wheels or spline knots.\n     - **`Full Tool` Mode**: Maximizes the grading interface for fine-tuning trackballs or curves without visual clutter.\n     - **`Full Scopes` Mode**: Expands the live analysis monitor for critical evaluation of RGB balance, skin tones, and dynamic range.\n\n2. **Embedded Real-Time Broadcast Scopes**:\n   - **Vectorscope**: Polar chrominance wheel with the 123\302\260 human skin-tone I-line and legal broadcast limit boxes.\n   - **RGB Waveform Parade**: 3-channel (Red, Green, Blue) parade showing black-level shadow lift and highlight roll-off across 0\342\200\223100 IRE.\n   - **RGB Histogram**: 256-bin continuous distribution curve.\n   - Quick one-tap switcher between Parade, Vectorscope, and Histogram.\n\n3. **Hosted Tool Consoles**:\n   - **Primary 3-Way Color Wheels Deck**: Horizontal-scrolling dock for Lift, Gamma, Gain, and Offset with 360\302\260 spectrum reticles and master luminance jog-wheel sliders.\n   - **Custom Spline Curves Editor**: 2D Cartesian curve canvas for Master, Red, Green, and Blue splines with interactive draggable knots.\n   - **3D LUT Browser**: Samsung Log profiles and custom `.cube` file loader.\n   - **Power Window Masking**: Radial and linear gradient mask controls with real-time feathering and invert toggles.\n   - **Film Look & FX**: Halation warm bloom, 35mm grain, vignette, and white balance