  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Masking Setup**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the existing masking implementation, specifically within `com`. The goal is to ascertain whether we can build upon our existing `MaskingOverlay` and augment it to handle elliptical and rectangular shapes, as part of the desired power window functionality. This will allow for localized color adjustments.\n\n\n**Defining Masking Types**\n\nI\'ve been defining the `MaskType` enum, realizing we need `ELLIPTICAL` and `RECTANGULAR`, alongside `LINEAR`. I also see that `PowerWindowMask` data class has the necessary fields for center, radii (x, y), rotation, feathering, and invert. Considering on-screen interaction, I\'m thinking about interactive handles for resizing, repositioning, and rotation. This will be the key to supporting user-driven power window creation on the overlay.\n\n\n**Implementing Masking Visualization**\n\nI\'m now focused on visualizing the mask interactions. I\'m planning a feathered boundary outline to show soft edge falloff, alongside visual dimming or a zebra pattern overlay for preview. Thinking about the implementation in `SamsungLogColorScience.evaluateMask()`, especially for the rectangular mask evaluation, I\'m considering using the signed distance to the box edges for the feathering calculation. This is moving toward the UI component.\n\n\n\n"
