  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining MaskType Enhancements**\n\nI\'m currently updating the `MaskType` enum. I\'ve added a `showMatte` boolean and have included `NONE`, `ELLIPTICAL`, `RECTANGULAR`, and `LINEAR` as the initial mask options. I\'m considering backward compatibility, so I\'ve created the alias `RADIAL = ELLIPTICAL` within the companion object.\n\n\n**Refining Mask Evaluation**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `evaluateMask` function within `SamsungLogColorScience.kt`. The current implementation handles `MaskType.NONE` and `ELLIPTICAL` cases, and I\'m ensuring the logic for rotation and radius calculations is sound. I\'m focusing on incorporating the `PowerWindowMask`\'s properties effectively, considering feathering and inner radius to properly shape the mask\'s impact.\n\n\n**Implementing MaskType Linear**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `MaskType.LINEAR` functionality within the `evaluateMask` function. I\'ve added the logic to handle the linear mask. I\'ve also incorporated a smoothstep function. I\'ve added a check to ensure that the radius values are clamped, preventing any issues in the mask calculation.\n\n\n**Adding Mask Visualizations**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to visualize the masks. I\'m focusing on the code within `SamsungLogColorScience.kt` regarding mask feathering and invert. I\'ve been considering how to render the black-and-white alpha mask preview in `gradeBitmap` to provide an accurate inspection of feathered boundaries. I also plan to create a `MaskingOverlay.kt` component to render interactive graphics over the video preview.\n\n\n**Visualizing Mask Controls**\n\nI\'m now designing the user interface elements for mask manipulation. I envision a crosshair reticle for repositioning, edge handles for independent resizing, and corner handles for proportional scaling. I\'m also adding a rotation handle. For the rectangular mask, I\'m thinking of a solid main rectangle with a dashed feathered outline. The linear mask will have a horizon line with upper and lower feather boundary lines.\n\n\n"
