aWithJavac NO-SOURCE> Task :app:processDebugUnitTestJavaRes UP-TO-DATE> Task :app:testDebugUnitTestBUILD SUCCESSFUL in 18s33 actionable tasks: 5 executed, 28 up-to-dateConfiguration cache entry reused.\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>### Built the \'MaskingOverlay\' Feature for Power Windows\n\nThe **`MaskingOverlay`** feature (`app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/MaskingOverlay.kt`) has been created and integrated over the video preview, enabling localized color adjustments with tactile DaVinci Resolve-style Power Windows:\n\n---\n\n#### Key Capabilities & Features:\n\n1. **Elliptical & Rectangular Power Windows**:\n   - **`MaskType.ELLIPTICAL`**:\n     - Solid boundary line for the primary ellipse.\n     - Cyan dashed outer ring displaying the feathered soft-edge falloff threshold.\n     - 4 directional handles (N, S, E, W) to scale width and height independently, plus 4 diagonal corner handles.\n     - Center crosshair reticle for direct on-screen translation.\n   - **`MaskType.RECTANGULAR`**:\n     - Solid rounded-corner rectangle boundary.\n     - Outer dashed cyan feathering border.\n     - 4 corner sizing squares and 4 midpoint edge circles for freeform aspect ratio adjustment.\n     - Center crosshair reticle for repositioning.\n   - **`MaskType.LINEAR`**:\n     - Center horizon guide with upper and lower feathered gradient boundaries.\n\n2. **Direct Touch Interactions on the Video Preview**:\n   - **Translate**: Tap and drag anywhere inside or on the center crosshair to reposition the window across the video frame.\n   - **Multi-Axis Sizing**: Drag horizontal or vertical handles to adjust width and height independently.\n   - **Double-Tap Reset**: Double-tap on the preview window to immediately reset the power window to default center and proportions.\n\n3. **Floating HUD Controls**:\n   - Quick one-tap switcher between **Elliptical**, **Rectangular**, **Linear**, and **Off**.\n   - **Invert Toggle**: Switch between grading inside the power window (e.g. subject relighting) vs. grading outside (e.g. background vignette/darkening).\n   - **Alpha Matte Mode (`Shift + H` Highlight)**: Renders a black-and-white alpha preview on the video monitor to verify edge falloff and feathering.\n\n4. **Synchronized Dock Controls**:\n   - In the Studio Dock, the Power Window panel exposes continuous sliders for **Width**, **Height**, and **Feather**, keeping on-canvas gestures and numeric adjustments in sync."
