  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Undo/Redo System**\n\nI\'m focusing on incorporating an undo/redo stack manager. I\'m imagining how it would track changes in color wheels, curves, and masks, essential for a professional grading setup. I\'m exploring the implications for efficient workflow.\n\n\n**Implementing History Stack**\n\nI\'ve been working on the history stack data structure, `UndoRedoManager<ColorGradeSettings>`. I\'ve added functions like `pushSnapshot()`, `canUndo`, `undo()`, etc. I\'m also considering memory limits for the history. Crucially, I\'m thinking about debouncing or using explicit \"commitChange()\" to avoid overwhelming the stack with unnecessary snapshots during continuous interactions like dragging color wheels.\n\n\n"
