  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Undo/Redo**\n\nI\'m currently designing an UndoRedoManager, and the data class `HistoryEntry` seems promising. It\'ll store `ColorGradeSettings` and a descriptive string. The settings can be updated via `updateSettings(transform)` which then updates the internal `_gradeSettings.value` variable. The data model is coming together well.\n\n\n**Implementing Undo/Redo**\n\nI\'ve implemented the `UndoRedoManager` class, complete with `undoStack` and `redoStack`. I\'m handling the history limit and preventing identical entries. The `pushState`, `undo`, `redo`, `canUndo`, and `canRedo` functions are now in place, and I think they\'re functioning correctly. I\'m excited to test them more thoroughly now!\n\n\n**Considering Drag Gestures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how continuous drag gestures should be handled within `GradingViewModel`. During the drag, I\'ll update settings in real-time, recording history disabled, for a smooth 60fps experience. Upon commit \342\200\223 either at the end of the gesture, after a short pause, or with discrete actions, I\'ll commit a history snapshot to the `UndoRedoManager`. I\'m using `updateSettingsWithDebounce` for this, to capture those final, key states.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_185075"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"package com.example.model\\n\\ndata class HistoryEntry(\\n    val settings: ColorGradeSettings,\\n    val description: String,\\n    val timestamp: Long = System.currentTimeMillis()\\n)\\n\\n/**\\n * Professional Undo/Redo stack manager designed for non-destructive color grading.\\n * Maintains history checkpoints across color wheels, curves, LUTs, and masking overlays.\\n */\\nclass UndoRedoManager(\\n    private val maxHistory: Int = 50\\n) {\\n    private val undoStack = mutableListOf<HistoryEntry>()\\n    private val redoStack = mutableListOf<HistoryEntry>()\\n\\n    init {\\n        undoStack.add(HistoryEntry(ColorGradeSettings(), \\\"Initial Grade\\\"))\\n    }\\n\\n    val canUndo: Boolean\\n        get() = undoStack.size > 1\\n\\n    val canRedo: Boolean\\n        get() = redoStack.isNotEmpty()\\n\\n    val historyEntries: List<HistoryEntry>\\n        get() = undoStack.toList()\\n\\n    val currentDescription: String\\n        get() = undoStack.lastOrNull()?.description ?: \\\"Initial Grade\\\"\\n\\n    /**\\n     * Push a new state snapshot to the undo stack, clearing any redos.\\n     */\\n    fun pushSnapshot(settings: ColorGradeSettings, description: String) {\\n        if (undoStack.isNotEmpty() && undoStack.last().settings == settings) {\\n            return // Skip duplicate states\\n        }\\n        undoStack.add(HistoryEntry(settings, description))\\n        if (undoStack.size > maxHistory) {\\n            undoStack.removeAt(0)\\n        }\\n        redoStack.clear()\\n    }\\n\\n    /**\\n     * Undo the last change and return the previous settings state.\\n     */\\n    fun undo(): HistoryEntry? {\\n        if (!canUndo) return null\\n        val current = undoStack.removeAt(undoStack.lastIndex)\\n        redoStack.add(current)\\n        return undoStack.lastOrNull()\\n    }\\n\\n    /**\\n     * Redo the undone change and return the restored settings state.\\n     */\\n    fun redo(): HistoryEntry? {\\n        if (!canRedo) return null\\n        val target = redoStack.removeAt(redoStack.lastIndex)\\n        undoStack.add(target)\\n        return target\\n    }\\n\\n    /**\\n     * Jump directly to a specific historical checkpoint.\\n     */\\n    fun jumpTo(entry: HistoryEntry): ColorGradeSettings? {\\n        val index = undoStack.indexOf(entry)\\n        if (index == -1) return null\\n\\n        while (undoStack.size > index + 1) {\\n            val popped = undoStack.removeAt(undoStack.lastIndex)\\n            redoStack.add(popped)\\n        }\\n        return undoStack.lastOrNull()?.settings\\n    }\\n\\n    /**\\n     * Reset the history stack with a fresh initial baseline.\\n     */\\n    fun reset(initialSettings: ColorGradeSettings = ColorGradeSettings()) {\\n        undoStack.clear()\\n        redoStack.clear()\\n        undoStack.add(HistoryEntry(initialSettings, \\\"Reset Grade\\\"))\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"Description\":\"Create UndoRedoManager.kt with history snapshots, stack depth management, undo, redo, and history jumping\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/app/src/main/java/com/example/model/UndoRedoManager.kt\",\"toolAction\":\"Writing UndoRedoManager.kt\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create undo/redo stack manager\"}"
