    thinking: "**Designing UI Controls**\n\nI\'m currently focused on implementing the Undo/Redo UI controls within `GradingStudioScreen.kt`. I\'ve started by integrating an Undo button (using `Icons.Default.Undo`) into the `TopAppBar`, making it conditionally enabled based on `canUndo`. Following the same pattern, I\'m adding a Redo button, employing `Icons.Default.Redo` and `canRedo` to dictate its enabled state.\n\n\n**Adding History Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating a history list button, using `Icons.Default.History`. This will trigger a slide-over or dialog displaying snapshots chronologically, highlighting the current state. Users can tap snapshots to jump to them. I\'ve also outlined action feedback: floating snackbars for Undo/Redo actions, showing descriptions like \"Undo: Adjust Lift.\" Furthermore, I\'ll be implementing specific descriptive labels when calling `updateSettings`, such as \"Adjust Lift (Shadows).\" A \"Reset\" button will now trigger a snapshot labeled \"Reset Grade.\"\n\n\n"
