  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User\'s Request**: Build a mobile color grading application inspired by DaVinci Resolve, specially tuned for Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra Pro Video 10-bit Log 4K footage.\n- **Latest Specific Instructions**:\n  1. Create a dedicated \'LUT Manager\' component with a built-in library of color transformation LUTs specifically optimized for mapping Samsung S24 Ultra Log footage to Rec.709.\n  2. Include a preview toggle (instant A/B compare and thumbnail look previews) and the ability to add/create different LUTs (custom user LUT creation and .cube import/export).\n  3. Ensure a real-time responsive histogram with RGB & luminance distribution and clipping warnings.\n  4. Ensure the entire application is fully mobile-responsive across different screen sizes, orientations, and aspect ratios.\n- **Target Identifiers & Scope**:\n  - App Name: `ResolveStudio`\n  - Application ID: `com.aistudio.colorgrader.samsunglog`\n  - Workspace: Jetpack Compose + Kotlin on Android SDK 36.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed Components & Code**:\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/model/ColorGradeState.kt`: Data structures for `WheelValue`, `CurvePoint`, `RgbCurves`, `PowerWindowMask` (with `MaskType.ELLIPTICAL`, `RECTANGULAR`, `LINEAR`, and `showMatte`), `FilmEffects`, `LutPreset`, and `ColorGradeSettings`.\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/model/UndoRedoManager.kt`: Bounded stack (50 entries) with history checkpoints, undo, redo, and direct jump-to functionality.\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/color/SamsungLogColorScience.kt`: Logarithmic decompression from Samsung Log to Linear, highlight knee roll-off, Rec.709 transform, monotonic cubic spline LUT generator, Lift/Gamma/Gain/Offset math, mask evaluator with elliptical and rectangular bounding algorithms, and `.cube` parser/generator.\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/video/SampleMediaGenerator.kt`: 4 HDR test scenes (Sunset Portrait, Tokyo Neon City, Alpine Vista, Film Noir Studio) with authentic flat 10-bit log gamma.\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/video/VideoExporter.kt`: MediaCodec + MediaMuxer H.264 video rendering, still PNG frame export, `.cube` 3D LUT export, and `FileProvider` share intent.\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/ColorWheel.kt`: Reusable Lift/Gamma/Gain/Offset color wheel with dynamic HSV tint glow, radial saturation vector, concentric graticules, fine-tune precision mode, and master luminance jog-wheel.\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/CurvesEditor.kt`: Master Y, Red, Green, Blue spline curve editor with draggable knots.\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/ScopesView.kt`: Live RGB Waveform Parade, Vectorscope (123\302\260 skin tone line), and 256-bin RGB Histogram.\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/MaskingOverlay.kt`: Interactive canvas overlay over video preview supporting elliptical & rectangular power windows, corner/edge resize handles, center reticle, and quick HUD.\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/PowerWindowOverlay.kt`: Dock controls for shape selection, width/height radius, feathering, invert, and alpha matte view.\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/StudioDockContainer.kt`: Layout container hosting wheels, curves, LUTs, mask, and real-time scopes with split-view and full-monitor modes.\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/HistoryDialog.kt`: Chronological history dialog with one-tap state rollback.\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/GradingViewModel.kt`: ViewModel managing real-time playback, debounced history snapshotting, media picking, and export jobs.\n  - `app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/GradingStudioScreen.kt`: Main UI integrating top app bar (Undo, Redo, History badge, Scenes, Export), video viewport with split wipe, dock container, and modals.\n  - Unit Tests: `app/src/test/java/com/example/ExampleUnitTest.kt` and `app/src/test/java/com/example/ExampleRobolectricTest.kt`.\n- **Verification Outcomes**:\n  - `compile_applet`: Completed with `Build succeeded` (most recent compile passed).\n  - `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest`: Passed with `BUILD SUCCESSFUL` (all 6 unit tests green).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- **Samsung Log Specifics**: Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra Pro Video records in 10-bit HEVC with logarithmic gamma ($y = a \\cdot \\ln(x \\cdot b + c) + d$), black point elevated to ~0.12\342\200\2230.15, and highlights preserved in the upper shoulder. Decompression is $x = \\frac{\\exp((y - d)/a) - c}{b}$ followed by highlight roll-off knee compression.\n- **Gesture Performance**: Continuous dragging of color wheels or curve points must update state immediately for 60fps rendering, while debouncing history stack snapshots (350ms) to ensure single-step undo per user interaction.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes (Exhaustive Session History)\n1. `generate_image` quota error (`generic::resource_exhausted`):\n   - *Fix*: Handled per `app-icon-generation` fallback rule by creating vector assets (`ic_launcher_foreground.xml` and `ic_launcher_background.xml`) and rendering mipmap PNGs using ImageMagick `convert`.\n2. Missing PIL python dependency when rendering icons:\n   - *Fix*: Switched to ImageMagick `convert` CLI in `run_command` per skill Option B.\n3. `ExampleRobolectricTest` failed asserting string `\"My Application\"`:\n   - *Fix*: Updated test to assert `\"ResolveStudio\"` after updating `res/values/strings.xml`.\n4. Monotonicity failure in `testSamsungLogToLinear`:\n   - *Root cause*: Piecewise condition had an arbitrary `y / slope` branch.\n   - *Fix*: Replaced with exact continuous exponential inverse $x = \\frac{\\exp((y - d)/a) - c}{b}$.\n5. Kotlin compiler errors in `MaskingOverlay.kt` and `GradingStudioScreen.kt`:\n   - *Root cause*: Missing imports (`border`, `expandVertically`, `shrinkVertically`, `FontFamily`) and extra closing braces.\n   - *Fix*: Added imports and corrected brace structure; subsequent compile succeeded.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- Current task in progress: Upgrading the LUT subsystem into a comprehensive `LutManager.kt` component with expanded Samsung S24 Log -> Rec.709 profiles, preview toggle, user custom LUT creation, real-time histogram integration, and mobile responsiveness audit.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps (Actionable Priority Order)\n1. **Expand `LutPreset` enum in `ColorGradeState.kt`**:\n   - Add new profiles: `SAMSUNG_REC709_PUNCH`, `FILM_FUJI_ETERNA`, `BLEACH_BYPASS`, `MONOCHROME_NOIR`, `CYBER_NEON_NIGHT`, `VINTAGE_SEPIA`.\n   - Add user custom saved LUT state support (`customPresets: List<SavedLutPreset>`).\n2. **Implement Mathematical Look Transforms in `SamsungLogColorScience.kt`**:\n   - In `applyLutPreset`, add conversion branches for all new `LutPreset` entries.\n3. **Build `LutManager.kt` (`app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/LutManager.kt`)**:\n   - Built-in library grid/carousel of S24 Log -> Rec.709 LUTs with real-time preview thumbnails.\n   - 1-tap **Preview Toggle** (instant A/B compare with LUT bypassed vs applied).\n   - \"Save Current Grade as Custom LUT\" dialog/button allowing user to name and add custom LUTs to the library.\n   - Opacity/intensity slider (0%\342\200\223100%).\n   - `.cube` import and export actions.\n4. **Enhance Real-Time Histogram**:\n   - In `ScopesView.kt` / `HistogramCanvas`, add clipping indicators for crushed blacks (< 0 IRE) and blown highlights (> 100 IRE) with real-time RGB curve updates.\n5. **Mobile Responsiveness Verification & Polishing**:\n   - Check `GradingStudioScreen.kt` and `StudioDockContainer.kt` using `BoxWithConstraints` or adaptive height modifiers to guarantee comfortable layout on small phone screens (e.g. 5.5\"\342\200\2236.1\") and landscape orientation.\n6. **Verification**:\n   - Run `compile_applet`.\n   - Run `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest`.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Must use Kotlin and Jetpack Compose exclusively (M3 guidelines).\n- Dark studio theme palette (`#0C0E14` base, `#F59E0B` amber accent) must be preserved.\n- Never use dangerous permissions or hardcode external SDK keys.\n- Keep `MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API` in `metadata.json`.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_end: 292
