  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the scope for a \"LUT Manager\" component. It seems the user wants a tool that handles color transformation LUTs, optimized for Samsung S24 Ultra Log footage to Rec. I\'m exploring the implications of a built-in library of LUTs and how best to structure it for efficient mapping. I\'m considering the potential integration with existing color management workflows.\n\n\n**Adding New Luts**\n\nI\'m now integrating the ability to add and create new LUTs into the component. A preview toggle for .709 display is on my mind. The focus is on a mobile-responsive design, essential for on-the-go color adjustments. Real-time histogram display is also being considered to aid with precise adjustments. I\'m prioritizing user control and intuitive interaction.\n\n\n**Implementing LUT Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing features for adding, previewing, and managing LUTs. I\'m focusing on an instant A/B compare toggle, either a button or hold-to-compare function. I\'m also planning a live thumbnail preview strip for each LUT. The addition of \"Create/Save Current Grade as LUT\" modal and user-created LUT storage are being prioritized alongside import capabilities. A deletion function is also in the plans for added customizability.\n\n\n**Adding Export Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating the ability to export custom LUTs as standard `.cube` files. I am also working on adding an intensity slider with fine-tune reset functionality. I\'m checking the histogram in `ScopesView.kt` and `StudioDockContainer.kt` for real-time RGB channels, luminance overlay, clipping indicators, peak values, and IRE grid lines. I\'m also planning a persistent or quick-toggle real-time mini-histogram. Furthermore, I\'m ensuring the app is completely responsive across all phone screen sizes.\n\n\n"
