  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Responsive Layout**\n\nI\'m currently exploring how the UI renders across different screen sizes. I\'m focusing on the `BoxWithConstraints` composable, employing it within `innerPadding` to ensure the layout adapts seamlessly to both landscape and responsive screens. This approach lets me monitor how the UI components behave under varying constraints.\n\n\n**Implementing Split Screen**\n\nI\'ve just implemented a conditional split-screen layout. When the screen is wider than it is tall, and wider than a threshold, I now arrange the `VideoPlayerView` and `StudioDockContainer` side-by-side. Otherwise, these elements are stacked vertically in a scrollable column. I am using weights to adjust sizes of the two boxes.\n\n\n**Refining Split Screen UI**\n\nI\'ve refined the split-screen UI further. In landscape mode, the video player is now fixed on the left with its controls, while the color wheels, curves, and 3D LUT manager dock expand on the right. In portrait, the view scrolls vertically, neatly arranging everything. I\'m also examining the `SaveLutDialog` implementation to ensure its integration remains intuitive and functional within this responsive framework.\n\n\n"
