  planner_response {
    response: "### ResolveStudio \342\200\224 3D LUT Manager, Real-Time Histogram & Mobile Responsiveness\n\nThe 3D LUT system and real-time broadcast scopes have been upgraded for Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra Pro Video 10-bit Log footage:\n\n#### 1. Professional 3D LUT Manager (`LutManager.kt` & `SaveLutDialog.kt`)\n- **Samsung S24 Log \342\206\222 Rec.709 Library**:\n  - **S24 Log \342\206\222 Rec.709 Natural**: Colorimetric mathematical recovery with calibrated neutral white point.\n  - **S24 Vivid Punch**: Extended dynamic range expansion (+20% contrast, vibrant chroma pop, deep clean blacks).\n  - **S24 Cine Warm**: Golden-hour skin tone preservation with amber highlight shoulder.\n  - **Kodak 2383 Print Stock**: Cinema film print stock emulation with soft highlight knee roll-off and rich teal shadows.\n  - **Fuji Eterna 250D**: Low-contrast soft pastel tones with muted highlights and rich foliage greens.\n  - **Blockbuster Teal & Orange**: Hollywood complementary color separation.\n  - **Clean Commercial High-Key**: Crisp whites, neutral skin tones, and high dynamic clarity.\n  - **Silver Gelatin B&W**: High dynamic range black & white tonal curve with deep contrast and metallic highlights.\n  - **Cyberpunk Neon**: Electric cyan and magenta separation tuned for night cityscapes.\n  - **Vintage Warm Sepia**: Nostalgic golden-hour warm shadows with analog softness.\n- **Instant A/B Preview Toggle**:\n  - One-tap `[LUT ACTIVE (A) / BYPASS (B)]` toggle allowing immediate zero-latency comparison of the footage before and after applying the selected LUT without resetting any grade parameters.\n- **Custom User LUT Creation & Library**:\n  - Tap **\"Save LUT\"** in the LUT dock to bake the active primary wheels, curves, exposure, temperature, and tint into a reusable custom 3D LUT profile.\n  - Custom LUTs appear directly in the **\"My Custom LUTs\"** tab, complete with live color swatches and the ability to export as industry-standard `.cube` tables or delete.\n- **LUT Intensity Control**:\n  - Smooth 0%\342\200\223100% opacity slider with a one-tap 100% reset button.\n\n#### 2. Real-Time Broadcast Histogram & Telemetry HUD (`ScopesView.kt` & `SamsungLogColorScience.kt`)\n- **Multi-Channel Overlay**: Real-time rendering of Red, Green, and Blue distribution curves overlaid with a semi-transparent luminance area.\n- **IRE Graticule Lines**: Calibration markers for 0%, 25%, 50%, 75%, and 100% IRE legal broadcast range.\n- **Real-Time Clipping Warnings**:\n  - **Shadow Crush Warning**: Highlighted alert badge indicating percentage of pixels below 0 IRE (<1% luminance).\n  - **Highlight Blowout Warning**: Alert badge indicating percentage of pixels clipped above 100 IRE (>99% luminance).\n  - **Average Luminance Readout**: Live percentage display of average scene brightness.\n\n#### 3. Complete Mobile Responsiveness (`GradingStudioScreen.kt`)\n- **Portrait Mobile Mode**: Responsive vertical layout with a 16:9 monitor viewport, interactive playhead scrubber, A/B wipe handle, and a dock container with horizontal toolbars.\n- **Landscape Studio Mode**: Auto-adapts when rotated or on wider screens (>560dp) into a side-by-side console: full-size video monitor on the left and full-height studio dock on the right.\n- Touch targets conform to Material 3 standards (minimum 48dp)."
    modified_response: "### ResolveStudio \342\200\224 3D LUT Manager, Real-Time Histogram & Mobile Responsiveness\n\nThe 3D LUT system and real-time broadcast scopes have been upgraded for Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra Pro Video 10-bit Log footage:\n\n#### 1. Professional 3D LUT Manager (`LutManager.kt` & `SaveLutDialog.kt`)\n- **Samsung S24 Log \342\206\222 Rec.709 Library**:\n  - **S24 Log \342\206\222 Rec.709 Natural**: Colorimetric mathematical recovery with calibrated neutral white point.\n  - **S24 Vivid Punch**: Extended dynamic range expansion (+20% contrast, vibrant chroma pop, deep clean blacks).\n  - **S24 Cine Warm**: Golden-hour skin tone preservation with amber highlight shoulder.\n  - **Kodak 2383 Print Stock**: Cinema film print stock emulation with soft highlight knee roll-off and rich teal shadows.\n  - **Fuji Eterna 250D**: Low-contrast soft pastel tones with muted highlights and rich foliage greens.\n  - **Blockbuster Teal & Orange**: Hollywood complementary color separation.\n  - **Clean Commercial High-Key**: Crisp whites, neutral skin tones, and high dynamic clarity.\n  - **Silver Gelatin B&W**: High dynamic range black & white tonal curve with deep contrast and metallic highlights.\n  - **Cyberpunk Neon**: Electric cyan and magenta separation tuned for night cityscapes.\n  - **Vintage Warm Sepia**: Nostalgic golden-hour warm shadows with analog softness.\n- **Instant A/B Preview Toggle**:\n  - One-tap `[LUT ACTIVE (A) / BYPASS (B)]` toggle allowing immediate zero-latency comparison of the footage before and after applying the selected LUT without resetting any grade parameters.\n- **Custom User LUT Creation & Library**:\n  - Tap **\"Save LUT\"** in the LUT dock to bake the active primary wheels, curves, exposure, temperature, and tint into a reusable custom 3D LUT profile.\n  - Custom LUTs appear directly in the **\"My Custom LUTs\"** tab, complete with live color swatches and the ability to export as industry-standard `.cube` tables or delete.\n- **LUT Intensity Control**:\n  - Smooth 0%\342\200\223100% opacity slider with a one-tap 100% reset button.\n\n#### 2. Real-Time Broadcast Histogram & Telemetry HUD (`ScopesView.kt` & `SamsungLogColorScience.kt`)\n- **Multi-Channel Overlay**: Real-time rendering of Red, Green, and Blue distribution curves overlaid with a semi-transparent luminance area.\n- **IRE Graticule Lines**: Calibration markers for 0%, 25%, 50%, 75%, and 100% IRE legal broadcast range.\n- **Real-Time Clipping Warnings**:\n  - **Shadow Crush Warning**: Highlighted alert badge indicating percentage of pixels below 0 IRE (<1% luminance).\n  - **Highlight Blowout Warning**: Alert badge indicating percentage of pixels clipped above 100 IRE (>99% luminance).\n  - **Average Luminance Readout**: Live percentage display of average scene brightness.\n\n#### 3. Complete Mobile Responsiveness (`GradingStudioScreen.kt`)\n- **Portrait Mobile Mode**: Responsive vertical layout with a 16:9 monitor viewport, interactive playhead scrubber, A/B wipe handle, and a dock container with horizontal toolbars.\n- **Landscape Studio Mode**: Auto-adapts when rotated or on wider screens (>560dp) into a side-by-side console: full-size video monitor on the left and full-height studio dock on the right.\n- Touch targets conform to Material 3 standards (minimum 48dp)."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
