  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing UI Requirements**\n\nI\'m deep-diving into the user\'s requirements. My focus is on understanding the nuances of a responsive UI state manager. I\'m prioritizing the collapse of the studio dock into a floating action menu on smaller screens, while ensuring the video preview area remains full-width. Currently, I\'m breaking down \"responsive\" to identify the essential elements to deliver a seamless user experience.\n\n\n**Defining UI States**\n\nI\'ve been dissecting the responsive UI requirement, and I\'ve started defining critical states. I envision a `StudioUiStateManager` controlling screen classifications like \"Compact\" and \"Medium\". Dock Display Modes, such as \"DOCKED_EXPANDED,\" \"COLLAPSED_FAB,\" and \"EXPANDED_BOTTOM_SHEET,\" are crucial. Auto-collapsing is also essential, especially on smaller screens to maximize video preview space.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Immersive Video**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the immersive video view and manual dock toggles. The goal is a full-width video preview, no matter the screen size, with controls that overlay cleanly. On smaller screens, the user should be able to manually collapse/expand the dock using a \"Focus Video View\" button. A DaVinci Resolve-inspired floating action menu is key, dynamically showing active tool badges and quick tool access.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1696616121787583164"
