  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring Small Screens**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the interface adapts to smaller screens. I\'m imagining the video preview area taking full width when the studio dock is collapsed. The studio dock could transform into a Floating Action Menu, a Speed Dial or Floating Dock Pill, to give it another name. This allows optimal usage of the space.\n\n\n**Refining the Floating Dock**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how the floating dock will work. It needs to be anchored at the bottom, and collapse into a Resolve-themed pill or expandable FAB. This includes icons for the current tool, a tool selector, a quick-adjust sheet, and a full expand/collapse toggle. On small screens, the preview will be full width, with the dock drawer popping up as needed. For larger screens, it will keep it side by side unless the user prefers otherwise. Clean architecture is key with a `StudioUiStateManager.kt`.\n\n\n**Defining Screen Sizes**\n\nI\'ve been defining the screen size classes. I\'m structuring these as an enum with COMPACT, MEDIUM, and EXPANDED values based on pixel width. I\'m also creating another enum to track the `DockPresentationMode`, which can be DOCKED, COLLAPSED_FLOATING, or FLOATING_DRAWER. The `StudioUiStateManager.kt` class is taking shape, tracking both the screen size class and the dock presentation mode, with the initial state on smaller screens defaulting to a collapsed floating dock.\n\n\n**Implementing Dock Presentation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `DockPresentationMode` logic. I\'ve added `isFloatingMenuExpanded` and `isToolSheetOpen` state variables. There\'s also a `userExplicitMode` for manual overrides. The `updateScreenDimensions` function determines the `ScreenSizeClass` and adjusts the `dockMode` accordingly, defaulting to `COLLAPSED` for compact screens unless overridden.\n\n\n**Refining Dock Control**\n\nI\'m now implementing the dock\'s behavior with more granular control. My plan is to include `toggleDockCollapse`, `openToolSheet`, `closeToolSheet`, `toggleFloatingMenu`, and `closeFloatingMenu` functions. These will manage states like `isFloatingMenuExpanded` and `isToolSheetOpen`. The `userExplicitMode` variable is crucial for overriding automatic adjustments based on screen size, ensuring user control over the dock\'s presentation.\n\n\n**Designing Floating Tool Menus**\n\nI\'m now designing the floating menu\'s details. I envision an amber/slate floating pill or circular FAB displaying the active tool\'s icon, its name, and a badge. An \"Expand Dock\" button would allow the full dock to appear. I\'m focusing on a \"Quick Action\" \"Inspect/Grade\" button that opens the tool sheet directly, keeping the video preview full-width. When expanded, I picture spring-animated speed-dial options for primary wheels, custom curves, LUT manager, masks, scopes, and A/B bypass, along with a \"Expand to Full Dock\" option. Tapping a tool selects it and opens the floating tool sheet.\n\n\n**Visualizing Bottom Sheets**\n\nI\'m now visualizing a bottom sheet, a styled floating elevated panel, to contain the tool dock. It will be easily draggable, dismissible with an \"X\" or \"Done\" button, or toggled to a full dock. The key is that the full-width video preview will always be in the background, uninterrupted.\n\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_12011391709227100371"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"package com.example.ui.state\\n\\nimport androidx.compose.runtime.Composable\\nimport androidx.compose.runtime.getValue\\nimport androidx.compose.runtime.mutableStateOf\\nimport androidx.compose.runtime.remember\\nimport androidx.compose.runtime.setValue\\nimport androidx.compose.ui.unit.Dp\\nimport androidx.compose.ui.unit.dp\\n\\n/**\\n * Screen size classifications for adaptive studio layouts.\\n */\\nenum class ScreenSizeClass {\\n    COMPACT,    // Mobile phone portrait (< 600dp width)\\n    MEDIUM,     // Small tablet / phone landscape (600dp..840dp)\\n    EXPANDED    // Tablet landscape / desktop (>= 840dp)\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Presentation mode for the color grading Studio Dock.\\n */\\nenum class DockPresentationMode {\\n    /** Dock is placed statically in layout (stacked or side-by-side) */\\n    DOCKED,\\n\\n    /** Dock is collapsed into a floating action menu, giving video 100% full-width view */\\n    COLLAPSED_FLOATING,\\n\\n    /** Quick grading modal sheet popped up from the floating action menu */\\n    FLOATING_SHEET\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Responsive UI State Manager for ResolveStudio.\\n * Intelligently manages dock presentation between docked cards and floating action menus\\n * based on screen geometry and user preferences.\\n */\\nclass StudioUiStateManager(\\n    initialSizeClass: ScreenSizeClass = ScreenSizeClass.COMPACT\\n) {\\n    var screenSizeClass by mutableStateOf(initialSizeClass)\\n        private set\\n\\n    var dockMode by mutableStateOf(\\n        if (initialSizeClass == ScreenSizeClass.COMPACT) DockPresentationMode.COLLAPSED_FLOATING\\n        else DockPresentationMode.DOCKED\\n    )\\n        private set\\n\\n    var isFloatingMenuExpanded by mutableStateOf(false)\\n        private set\\n\\n    var isToolSheetOpen by mutableStateOf(false)\\n        private set\\n\\n    private var userExplicitPreference: DockPresentationMode? = null\\n\\n    /**\\n     * Updates screen dimensions and auto-adapts dock mode if user has not set an explicit override.\\n     */\\n    fun updateScreenDimensions(widthDp: Dp, heightDp: Dp) {\\n        val newClass = when {\\n            widthDp < 600.dp -> ScreenSizeClass.COMPACT\\n            widthDp < 840.dp -> ScreenSizeClass.MEDIUM\\n            else -> ScreenSizeClass.EXPANDED\\n        }\\n\\n        if (newClass != screenSizeClass) {\\n            screenSizeClass = newClass\\n            if (userExplicitPreference == null) {\\n                dockMode = if (newClass == ScreenSizeClass.COMPACT) {\\n                    DockPresentationMode.COLLAPSED_FLOATING\\n                } else {\\n                    DockPresentationMode.DOCKED\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /**\\n     * Toggles between docked container mode and collapsed floating action menu.\\n     */\\n    fun toggleDockMode() {\\n        if (dockMode == DockPresentationMode.COLLAPSED_FLOATING) {\\n            userExplicitPreference = DockPresentationMode.DOCKED\\n            dockMode = DockPresentationMode.DOCKED\\n            isToolSheetOpen = false\\n            isFloatingMenuExpanded = false\\n        } else {\\n            userExplicitPreference = DockPresentationMode.COLLAPSED_FLOATING\\n            dockMode = DockPresentationMode.COLLAPSED_FLOATING\\n            isToolSheetOpen = false\\n            isFloatingMenuExpanded = false\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /**\\n     * Explicitly collapse dock into floating menu to maximize video preview area.\\n     */\\n    fun collapseToFloating() {\\n        userExplicitPreference = DockPresentationMode.COLLAPSED_FLOATING\\n        dockMode = DockPresentationMode.COLLAPSED_FLOATING\\n        isToolSheetOpen = false\\n        isFloatingMenuExpanded = false\\n    }\\n\\n    /**\\n     * Explicitly expand dock into layout.\\n     */\\n    fun expandToDocked() {\\n        userExplicitPreference = DockPresentationMode.DOCKED\\n        dockMode = DockPresentationMode.DOCKED\\n        isToolSheetOpen = false\\n        isFloatingMenuExpanded = false\\n    }\\n\\n    fun openToolSheet() {\\n        isToolSheetOpen = true\\n        isFloatingMenuExpanded = false\\n    }\\n\\n    fun closeToolSheet() {\\n        isToolSheetOpen = false\\n    }\\n\\n    fun toggleFloatingMenu() {\\n        isFloatingMenuExpanded = !isFloatingMenuExpanded\\n    }\\n\\n    fun closeFloatingMenu() {\\n        isFloatingMenuExpanded = false\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n@Composable\\nfun rememberStudioUiStateManager(\\n    initialSizeClass: ScreenSizeClass = ScreenSizeClass.COMPACT\\n): StudioUiStateManager {\\n    return remember { StudioUiStateManager(initialSizeClass) }\\n}\\n\",\"Description\":\"Create StudioUiStateManager to manage responsive dock collapse and floating action menu states\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/state/StudioUiStateManager.kt\",\"toolAction\":\"Writing StudioUiStateManager\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create StudioUiStateManager class\"}"
