  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Bottom Bar Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the rendering logic of the `bottomBar`. Specifically, I\'m noting how the `dockMode` from `uiStateManager` affects its behavior. When `dockMode` is `DOCKED`, I plan to render `StudioDockTabs`. If, however, `dockMode` is `COLLAPSED_FLOATING`, the bottom bar goes away entirely, which will be useful.\n\n\n**Integrating Toggle Actions**\n\nI\'ve integrated a dock presentation toggle button into the `TopAppBar`\'s actions. It cleverly shifts between a `Dock` icon and a `CloseFullscreen` icon based on the `dockMode`. The button\'s behavior, which is handled via a state manager and tests, intuitively swaps between floating and docked views. I also am now able to update screen dimensions for the `BoxWithConstraints`.\n\n\n**Defining Collapsed Layout**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the layout when `dockMode` is `COLLAPSED_FLOATING`. The `Box` covers the full size, and the `Column` with a vertical scroll and padding. This should allow space for the floating menu and a viewport for the video player. I can now properly adjust the screen dimensions.\n\n\n**Refining Floating Menu**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `StudioFloatingActionMenu` component, considering how to handle its visibility. Specifically, I\'m integrating logic to toggle its expanded state and select tabs. I have also added functionality for opening a tool sheet, expanding to a docked state, and toggling bypass settings. Now, I will implement its conditional rendering based on the `uiStateManager.isToolSheetOpen`.\n\n\n"
