dioFloatingActionMenu` when the dock is in floating mode. I\'m also observing the interaction of the `onBypassToggle` callback to update the settings based on the current state and how it affects the visual settings. I\'m noting the use of window insets to manage positioning. I am seeing the layout shift to consider `DockPresentationMode.DOCKED`.\n\n\n**Scrutinizing Callbacks**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the callbacks within the UI, specifically how `onMaskChange`, `onPlayPauseToggle`, and `onSeek` are utilized. The `updateSettings` call with description \"Adjust Power Window\" is noteworthy. I\'m also looking at the `StudioDock` composable, and its role in this layout. The `Box` modifiers are under consideration.\n\n\n**Scoping Functionality**\n\nI\'m now examining how the UI state manager handles the transition to a floating state from a docked state using `onCollapseToFloating()`. The `Container` composable now holds my focus as it is responsible for the collapse functionality. I am investigating the callback for `onSettingsChange` now. The `onCreateCustomLutClick`, and `onDeleteCustomLut` are worth noting for file handling. Finally, I\'m noting the portrait mobile mode as well.\n\n\n**Observing Video Playback**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `VideoPlayerView` composable and its interactions. I\'m noting the data bindings for video playback including `gradedBitmap`, `rawBitmap`, and the playback state variables. I\'m focusing on how callbacks such as `onMaskChange`, `onPlayPauseToggle`, and `onSeek` are utilized to interact with the view model. I need to understand how these elements are connected and how the view model updates the UI state. I see the spacer adds padding.\n\n\n\n**Analyzing Tool Sheet Integration**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `StudioDock` composable and observing how the `StudioFloatingToolSheet` is conditionally displayed based on `uiStateManager.isToolSheetOpen`. I see how `onTabSelected`, `settings`, `onSettingsChange`, and other callbacks are passed and utilized. I\'m focusing on the interaction between the `uiStateManager` and the visibility of this tool sheet, especially how the callbacks trigger changes to the view model and, by extension, the user interface. I need to understand this conditional rendering.\n\n\n\n"
