  planner_response {
    response: "### Responsive UI State Manager & Collapsible Floating Studio Dock\n\nA responsive UI state manager has been implemented to keep the 4K video preview area **100% full-width** and distraction-free on smaller mobile screens while collapsing the Studio Dock into an interactive Floating Action Menu (Speed Dial):\n\n---\n\n#### 1. Responsive UI State Manager (`StudioUiStateManager.kt`)\n- **Screen Geometry Adaptation**:\n  - **`COMPACT` (< 600dp width)**: Automatically collapses the heavy studio dock into the sleek floating action menu, maximizing the video viewport width and vertical display.\n  - **`MEDIUM` / `EXPANDED` ($\\ge$ 600dp / Landscape)**: Automatically transitions into docked console mode (stacked or side-by-side).\n- **Presentation Modes (`DockPresentationMode`)**:\n  - `COLLAPSED_FLOATING`: Studio dock collapses into a floating action pill anchored to the screen\'s bottom-end, freeing up the entire stage for the video preview and A/B split-wipe inspection.\n  - `DOCKED`: Traditional dock layout with the primary color wheels, spline curves, 3D LUT manager, power window mask, and broadcast scopes.\n  - `FLOATING_SHEET`: Temporary modal sheet allowing quick precision adjustments without permanently taking away screen real estate.\n- **Manual Overrides**: Users can toggle between floating and docked mode at any time via the TopAppBar button or the collapse icon in the dock header.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Studio Floating Action Menu & Speed Dial (`StudioFloatingActionMenu.kt`)\n- **Main Floating HUD Pill**:\n  - Amber-accented floating pill displaying the active tool icon (Wheels, Curves, 3D LUTs, Power Window, Scopes), title, and one-tap grading access.\n  - Anchored with navigation bar inset padding (`WindowInsets.navigationBars`) to prevent notch or system navigation gesture conflicts.\n- **Speed Dial Menu**:\n  - **Expand Dock**: One-tap action to un-collapse into the full docked layout.\n  - **A/B Bypass Toggle**: Quick toggle to compare raw vs graded footage in full-width view.\n  - **Tool Selectors**: Direct buttons for Primary Wheels, Custom Curves, 3D LUT Manager, Power Window, and Film Looks & FX.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Floating Tool Sheet Modal (`StudioFloatingToolSheet.kt`)\n- Tapping any tool from the floating action menu opens a responsive bottom sheet containing the studio dock controls.\n- Allows precision touch grading on wheels, curves, and LUTs, and can be dismissed with a swipe or tap when finished, returning to the full-width video view.\n- Includes an **\"Expand to Screen\"** button to pin the dock if the user wants it permanent."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Output**\n\nI\'ve just finished running all tests and the build was successful in 18 seconds! Now I\'m reviewing the output, specifically `StudioUiStateManager.kt`. I\'m paying close attention to the ScreenSizeClass detection logic. It looks like it\'s correctly identifying COMPACT screens as under 600dp and MEDIUM screens between 600 and some upper limit.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Responsive UI State Manager & Collapsible Floating Studio Dock\n\nA responsive UI state manager has been implemented to keep the 4K video preview area **100% full-width** and distraction-free on smaller mobile screens while collapsing the Studio Dock into an interactive Floating Action Menu (Speed Dial):\n\n---\n\n#### 1. Responsive UI State Manager (`StudioUiStateManager.kt`)\n- **Screen Geometry Adaptation**:\n  - **`COMPACT` (< 600dp width)**: Automatically collapses the heavy studio dock into the sleek floating action menu, maximizing the video viewport width and vertical display.\n  - **`MEDIUM` / `EXPANDED` ($\\ge$ 600dp / Landscape)**: Automatically transitions into docked console mode (stacked or side-by-side).\n- **Presentation Modes (`DockPresentationMode`)**:\n  - `COLLAPSED_FLOATING`: Studio dock collapses into a floating action pill anchored to the screen\'s bottom-end, freeing up the entire stage for the video preview and A/B split-wipe inspection.\n  - `DOCKED`: Traditional dock layout with the primary color wheels, spline curves, 3D LUT manager, power window mask, and broadcast scopes.\n  - `FLOATING_SHEET`: Temporary modal sheet allowing quick precision adjustments without permanently taking away screen real estate.\n- **Manual Overrides**: Users can toggle between floating and docked mode at any time via the TopAppBar button or the collapse icon in the dock header.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Studio Floating Action Menu & Speed Dial (`StudioFloatingActionMenu.kt`)\n- **Main Floating HUD Pill**:\n  - Amber-accented floating pill displaying the active tool icon (Wheels, Curves, 3D LUTs, Power Window, Scopes), title, and one-tap grading access.\n  - Anchored with navigation bar inset padding (`WindowInsets.navigationBars`) to prevent notch or system navigation gesture conflicts.\n- **Speed Dial Menu**:\n  - **Expand Dock**: One-tap action to un-collapse into the full docked layout.\n  - **A/B Bypass Toggle**: Quick toggle to compare raw vs graded footage in full-width view.\n  - **Tool Selectors**: Direct buttons for Primary Wheels, Custom Curves, 3D LUT Manager, Power Window, and Film Looks & FX.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Floating Tool Sheet Modal (`StudioFloatingToolSheet.kt`)\n- Tapping any tool from the floating action menu opens a responsive bottom sheet containing the studio dock controls.\n- Allows precision touch grading on wheels, curves, and LUTs, and can be dismissed with a swipe or tap when finished, returning to the full-width video view.\n- Includes an **\"Expand to Screen\"** button to pin the dock if the user wants it permanent."
