  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Embedding Film Grain Controls**\n\nI\'m currently working on integrating `FilmGrainControls` within `EffectsPanel.kt`. The goal is to refactor Section 3, specifically incorporating film grain adjustments into the existing structure to create a more functional and user-friendly interface. I\'m focusing on ensuring it aligns properly within the `Row` layout and maintaining the vertical alignment.\n\n\n**Refining Film Grain Section**\n\nI\'ve just added the \"ANALOG FILM EFFECTS\" section with a visual header to the interface, which should improve its overall aesthetic. I\'ve also incorporated the `FilmGrainControls`, allowing for direct adjustment of the grain settings.  I\'m pleased with the alignment within the panel layout, and the implementation of a dedicated organic film grain processor. I\'m making sure it\342\200\231s integrated with the relevant settings change handler.\n\n\n**Adding Halation & Vignette Sliders**\n\nI\'ve just implemented the \"Halation Glow\" and \"Vignette\" sliders within the interface, using `GradeSliderRow`. These sliders provide direct control over halation and vignette intensity, with the updated values reflected using a settings change handler. I\'ve focused on ensuring they are properly formatted with their own unique tags, which enables easy testing.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_12713181673212772011"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Integrate FilmGrainControls into EffectsPanel\",\"EndLine\":196,\"Instruction\":\"Embed FilmGrainControls in EffectsPanel with controls for size, roughness, and strength\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"            // Section 3: Film Halation, Grain Processor & Vignette\\n            Row(verticalAlignment = Alignment.CenterVertically) {\\n                Icon(Icons.Default.AutoAwesome, contentDescription = null, tint = ResolveAmber, modifier = Modifier.size(14.dp))\\n                Spacer(modifier = Modifier.width(6.dp))\\n                Text(\\n                    text = \\\"ANALOG FILM EFFECTS\\\",\\n                    color = TextPrimary,\\n                    fontSize = 10.sp,\\n                    fontWeight = FontWeight.Bold,\\n                    letterSpacing = 0.5.sp\\n                )\\n            }\\n            Spacer(modifier = Modifier.height(4.dp))\\n\\n            // Dedicated Organic Film Grain Processor\\n            FilmGrainControls(\\n                grain = settings.effects.grain,\\n                onGrainChange = { newGrain ->\\n                    onSettingsChange(\\n                        settings.copy(\\n                            effects = settings.effects.copy(\\n                                grain = newGrain,\\n                                grainIntensity = if (newGrain.enabled) newGrain.strength else 0f,\\n                                grainSize = newGrain.size\\n                            )\\n                        )\\n                    )\\n                },\\n                modifier = Modifier.fillMaxWidth()\\n            )\\n\\n            Spacer(modifier = Modifier.height(6.dp))\\n\\n            GradeSliderRow(\\n                label = \\\"Halation Glow\\\",\\n                value = settings.effects.halationIntensity,\\n                onValueChange = {\\n                    onSettingsChange(settings.copy(effects = settings.effects.copy(halationIntensity = it)))\\n                },\\n                valueRange = 0.0f..1.0f,\\n                activeColor = ResolveRed,\\n                formatString = \\\"%.2f\\\",\\n                testTag = \\\"halation_slider\\\"\\n            )\\n\\n            GradeSliderRow(\\n                label = \\\"Vignette\\\",\\n                value = settings.effects.vignetteIntensity,\\n                onValueChange = {\\n                    onSettingsChange(settings.copy(effects = settings.effects.copy(vignetteIntensity = it)))\\n                },\\n                valueRange = 0.0f..1.0f,\\n                activeColor = Color(0xFF64748B),\\n                formatString = \\\"%.2f\\\",\\n                testTag = \\\"vignette_slider\\\"\\n            )\",\"StartLine\":147,\"TargetContent\":\"            // Section 3: Film Halation, Grain & Vignette\\n            Row(verticalAlignment = Alignment.CenterVertically) {\\n                Icon(Icons.Default.AutoAwesome, contentDescription = null, tint = ResolveAmber, modifier = Modifier.size(14.dp))\\n                Spacer(modifier = Modifier.width(6.dp))\\n                Text(\\n                    text = \\\"ANALOG FILM EFFECTS\\\",\\n                    color = TextPrimary,\\n                    fontSize = 10.sp,\\n                    fontWeight = FontWeight.Bold,\\n                    letterSpacing = 0.5.sp\\n                )\\n            }\\n            Spacer(modifier = Modifier.height(4.dp))\\n\\n            GradeSliderRow(\\n                label = \\\"Halation Glow\\\",\\n                value = settings.effects.halationIntensity,\\n                onValueChange = {\\n                    onSettingsChange(settings.copy(effects = settings.effects.copy(halationIntensity = it)))\\n                },\\n                valueRange = 0.0f..1.0f,\\n                activeColor = ResolveRed,\\n                formatString = \\\"%.2f\\\",\\n                testTag = \\\"halation_slider\\\"\\n            )\\n\\n            GradeSliderR