  planner_response {
    response: "### Organic Film Grain Processor Implemented\n\nAn organic film grain processor modeling authentic physical film emulsion (silver halide crystals & dye cloud dispersion) has been created with real-time controls for **grain strength**, **size**, and **roughness**:\n\n---\n\n#### 1. Film Grain Processing Engine (`FilmGrainProcessor.kt`)\n- **Multi-Scale Organic Lattice Noise**:\n  - Replaces flat white noise with multi-octave coherent gradient noise that clusters into organic silver halide clumps rather than isolated digital pixels.\n- **Exposure-Dependent Emulsion Density Curve**:\n  - Grain naturally concentrates in the midtones ($4 \\times \\text{lum} \\times (1 - \\text{lum})$) and upper shadows where optical density transitions occur on real physical film, rolling off smoothly in saturated specular highlights and deep unexposed blacks.\n- **Roughness & Size Synthesis**:\n  - **Size ($0.5\\times$ to $3.0\\times$)**: Controls the physical crystal cluster scale (emulating $65\\text{mm}$ IMAX micro-grain vs $35\\text{mm}$ theatrical vs $16\\text{mm}$/$8\\text{mm}$ coarse stocks).\n  - **Roughness ($0.0$ to $1.0$)**: Blends smooth organic wave clumping with high-frequency crystalline micro-noise for grittier textures.\n- **Silver Halide vs Color Dye Cloud Emulation**:\n  - **Monochrome Silver**: Uniform luminance perturbation for authentic black-and-white silver grain.\n  - **Color Dye**: 3-layer channel-offset variation simulating color negative dye clouds.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Film Stock Presets (`FilmStockPreset`)\n- **35mm Kodak 50D**: Fine, tight grain structure with subtle roughness ($1.0\\times$ size, $0.35$ roughness, $28\\%$ strength).\n- **16mm Kodak 500T**: High-speed indie cinema grain with pronounced organic texture ($1.8\\times$ size, $0.70$ roughness, $55\\%$ strength).\n- **8mm Super 8**: Heavy vintage organic grain with prominent crystalline roughness ($2.6\\times$ size, $0.85$ roughness, $80\\%$ strength).\n- **65mm IMAX Pristine**: Micro-fine grain for ultra-clean cinematic resolution ($0.6\\times$ size, $0.20$ roughness, $16\\%$ strength).\n- **Custom Stock**: Full manual parameter control.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Interactive UI Controls (`FilmGrainControls.kt` & `EffectsPanel.kt`)\n- **Master Grain Switch**: One-tap toggle to enable or bypass grain.\n- **Live 100% Magnification Texture Loupe**:\n  - Real-time $160\\times 70$ preview swatch showing the exact synthesized organic grain texture as you slide Size, Roughness, and Strength.\n- **Dedicated Sliders**:\n  - **Strength**: $0\\%$ to $100\\%$ intensity slider.\n  - **Size**: $0.50\\times$ to $3.00\\times$ scale slider.\n  - **Roughness**: $0.00$ to $1.00$ texture grit slider.\n  - **Midtone Bias**: $0.20$ to $1.00$ emulsion response slider.\n  - **Monochrome / Color Dye** switch.\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Verification\n- Integrated with `gradeBitmap` pipeline and video exporter for real-time 60fps playback and MP4 exports.\n- Verified with unit tests (`testFilmGrainProcessorEmulsionDensity` and `testFilmGrainApplication`) and clean Gradle compilation."
    modified_response: "### Organic Film Grain Processor Implemented\n\nAn organic film grain processor modeling authentic physical film emulsion (silver halide crystals & dye cloud dispersion) has been created with real-time controls for **grain strength**, **size**, and **roughness**:\n\n---\n\n#### 1. Film Grain Processing Engine (`FilmGrainProcessor.kt`)\n- **Multi-Scale Organic Lattice Noise**:\n  - Replaces flat white noise with multi-octave coherent gradient noise that clusters into organic silver halide clumps rather than isolated digital pixels.\n- **Exposure-Dependent Emulsion Density Curve**:\n  - Grain naturally concentrates in the midtones ($4 \\times \\text{lum} \\times (1 - \\text{lum})$) and upper shadows where optical density transitions occur on real physical film, rolling off smoothly in saturated specular highlights and deep unexposed blacks.\n- **Roughness & Size Synthesis**:\n  - **Size ($0.5\\times$ to $3.0\\times$)**: Controls the physical crystal cluster scale (emulating $65\\text{mm}$ IMAX micro-grain vs $35\\text{mm}$ theatrical vs $16\\text{mm}$/$8\\text{mm}$ coarse stocks).\n  - **Roughness ($0.0$ to $1.0$)**: Blends smooth organic wave clumping with high-frequency crystalline micro-noise for grittier textures.\n- **Silver Halide vs Color Dye Cloud Emulation**:\n  - **Monochrome Silver**: Uniform luminance perturbation for authentic black-and-white silver grain.\n  - **Color Dye**: 3-layer channel-offset variation simulating color negative dye clouds.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Film Stock Presets (`FilmStockPreset`)\n- **35mm Kodak 50D**: Fine, tight grain structure with subtle roughness ($1.0\\times$ size, $0.35$ roughness, $28\\%$ strength).\n- **16mm Kodak 500T**: High-speed indie cinema grain with pronounced organic texture ($1.8\\times$ size, $0.70$ roughness, $55\\%$ strength).\n- **8mm Super 8**: Heavy vintage organic grain with prominent crystalline roughness ($2.6\\times$ size, $0.85$ roughness, $80\\%$ strength).\n- **65mm IMAX Pristine**: Micro-fine grain for ultra-clean cinematic resolution ($0.6\\times$ size, $0.20$ roughness, $16\\%$ strength).\n- **Custom Stock**: Full manual parameter control.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Interactive UI Controls (`FilmGrainControls.kt` & `EffectsPanel.kt`)\n- **Master Grain Switch**: One-tap toggle to enable or bypass grain.\n- **Live 100% Magnification Texture Loupe**:\n  - Real-time $160\\times 70$ preview swatch showing the exact synthesized organic grain texture as you slide Size, Roughness, and Strength.\n- **Dedicated Sliders**:\n  - **Strength**: $0\\%$ to $100\\%$ intensity slider.\n  - **Size**: $0.50\\times$ to $3.00\\times$ scale slider.\n  - **Roughness**: $0.00$ to $1.00$ texture grit slider.\n  - **Midtone Bias**: $0.20$ to $1.00$ emulsion response slider.\n  - **Monochrome / Color Dye** switch.\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Verification\n- Integrated with `gradeBitmap` pipeline and video exporter for real-time 60fps playback and MP4 exports.\n- Verified with unit tests (`testFilmGrainProcessorEmulsionDensity` and `testFilmGrainApplication`) and clean Gradle compilation."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\367\001\n\364\001\001i\024}\023M\tt\264N/\266~\365C\236@7\031\v\306\253\253^\037GB\214\254\326O\340\252\314\236\355\0023\017\360f\273\243LM\226?\244T\360E\"O\231\242\327R\324\346\016M\244t7Y\212\035\317wJ\n\245\206?;1\f\302\376\032~?\303\304}\372\224\270+\v\025\370\336\303\273\226\032z\274\3254\223\252\327\301\004Q\250\t\356<g$\0234\2359\f\231$d\360\370\225px\242i\231\376D\242\311\v\343+n\034\215\344\200\364/\254\310\343\264\n~J\3729\\=\332$k\207\323q6\230p\270\240^\307\356z\322\370\3410<\021u\362\317\254\364\024zmI\274\341\035\ve\355\350\327\342t\244u\264M~\340\\2A\201H1\001G!\270\271C\320F3A\f\355h\024\345\245\214Y\311\3627\021Zar\257\241\345v\325\021\214\021+\331/\022\236"
