    response: "### Organic Film Grain Processor Implemented\n\nAn authentic, physical-emulsion film grain processor has been created to overlay organic grain textures onto graded Samsung S24 Ultra footage with precise controls for **size**, **roughness**, and **strength**:\n\n---\n\n#### 1. Emulsion Texture Synthesis Engine (`FilmGrainProcessor.kt`)\n- **Multi-Scale Organic Clumping**:\n  - Replaces generic digital white noise with multi-octave coherent gradient noise that models physical silver halide crystal aggregation in photographic emulsion.\n- **Exposure-Dependent Emulsion Density**:\n  - Accurately simulates film optical response: grain density peaks in the midtones ($4 \\times L \\times (1-L)$ bell curve) and rolls off smoothly in saturated highlight shoulders and zero-exposure deep shadows.\n- **Roughness & Octave Blending**:\n  - Controls the ratio between smooth organic cluster clumping (low roughness) and sharp crystalline salt speckles (high roughness).\n- **Emulsion Types**:\n  - **Monochrome Silver Halide**: Applies balanced monochromatic density perturbations.\n  - **3-Layer Color Dye Cloud**: Simulates independent cyan, magenta, and yellow dye cloud fluctuations.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Dedicated UI Controls (`FilmGrainControls.kt` & `EffectsPanel.kt`)\n- **Master Grain Switch**: Easily toggle film grain on and off.\n- **Film Stock Presets**:\n  - **`35mm Kodak 50D`**: Fine particle size (1.0x), subtle roughness (0.35), moderate strength (28%).\n  - **`16mm Kodak 500T`**: Gritty indie look with larger organic grain (1.8x), higher roughness (0.70), and pronounced strength (55%).\n  - **`8mm Super 8`**: Heavy vintage analog clustering (2.6x size, 0.85 roughness, 80% strength).\n  - **`65mm IMAX Pristine`**: Ultra-fine micro-grain (0.6x size, 0.20 roughness, 16% strength).\n  - **`Custom Stock`**: Unlocks all sliders for custom creation.\n- **Live 100% Magnification Texture Loupe**:\n  - A real-time preview swatch that generates an authentic mid-gray texture sample of the exact current grain structure as sliders are manipulated.\n- **Core Sliders**:\n  - **Strength**: 0% to 100% overall intensity.\n  - **Size**: 0.50x to 3.00x particle cluster scaling.\n  - **Roughness**: 0.00 (smooth clumping) to 1.00 (sharp granular speckles).\n  - **Midtone Bias**: 0.20 to 1.00 emulsion concentration adjustment.\n  - **Monochrome Switch**: Toggle between silver halide and 3-channel color dye clouds.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Verification & Pipeline Integration\n- Fully integrated into `SamsungLogColorScience.gradeBitmap()` for live playback and 4K MP4 exports.\n- Verified with unit tests (`testFilmGrainProcessorEmulsionDensity`, `testFilmGrainApplication`) and clean build compilation."
    modified_response: "### Organic Film Grain Processor Implemented\n\nAn authentic, physical-emulsion film grain processor has been created to overlay organic grain textures onto graded Samsung S24 Ultra footage with precise controls for **size**, **roughness**, and **strength**:\n\n---\n\n#### 1. Emulsion Texture Synthesis Engine (`FilmGrainProcessor.kt`)\n- **Multi-Scale Organic Clumping**:\n  - Replaces generic digital white noise with multi-octave coherent gradient noise that models physical silver halide crystal aggregation in photographic emulsion.\n- **Exposure-Dependent Emulsion Density**:\n  - Accurately simulates film optical response: grain density peaks in the midtones ($4 \\times L \\times (1-L)$ bell curve) and rolls off smoothly in saturated highlight shoulders and zero-exposure deep shadows.\n- **Roughness & Octave Blending**:\n  - Controls the ratio between smooth organic cluster clumping (low roughness) and sharp crystalline salt speckles (high roughness).\n- **Emulsion Types**:\n  - **Monochrome Silver Halide**: Applies balanced monochromatic density perturbations.\n  - **3-Layer Color Dye Cloud**: Simulates independent cyan, magenta, and yellow dye cloud fluctuations.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Dedicated UI Controls (`FilmGrainControls.kt` & `EffectsPanel.kt`)\n- **Master Grain Switch**: Easily toggle film grain on and off.\n- **Film Stock Presets**:\n  - **`35mm Kodak 50D`**: Fine particle size (1.0x), subtle roughness (0.35), moderate strength (28%).\n  - **`16mm Kodak 500T`**: Gritty indie look with larger organic grain (1.8x), higher roughness (0.70), and pronounced strength (55%).\n  - **`8mm Super 8`**: Heavy vintage analog clustering (2.6x size, 0.85 roughness, 80% strength).\n  - **`65mm IMAX Pristine`**: Ultra-fine micro-grain (0.6x size, 0.20 roughness, 16% strength).\n  - **`Custom Stock`**: Unlocks all sliders for custom creation.\n- **Live 100% Magnification Texture Loupe**:\n  - A real-time preview swatch that generates an authentic mid-gray texture sample of the exact current grain structure as sliders are manipulated.\n- **Core Sliders**:\n  - **Strength**: 0% to 100% overall intensity.\n  - **Size**: 0.50x to 3.00x particle cluster scaling.\n  - **Roughness**: 0.00 (smooth clumping) to 1.00 (sharp granular speckles).\n  - **Midtone Bias**: 0.20 to 1.00 emulsion concentration adjustment.\n  - **Monochrome Switch**: Toggle between silver halide and 3-channel color dye clouds.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Verification & Pipeline Integration\n- Fully integrated into `SamsungLogColorScience.gradeBitmap()` for live playback and 4K MP4 exports.\n- Verified with unit tests (`testFilmGrainProcessorEmulsionDensity`, `testFilmGrainApplication`) and clean build compilation."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
