  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Preset Storage**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the UI design aspect for saving custom grading configurations as user presets. The goal is to make it intuitive for users to save and quickly apply their preferred looks to different clips, keeping the storage mechanism efficient and accessible within the grading interface.\n\n\n**Evaluating Persistence Options**\n\nI\'ve been re-evaluating the best way to store these presets. After checking our existing dependencies, it looks like we\'re already using Room, which is great! That simplifies things considerably. I\'m leaning toward using local persistence via Room, considering the user\'s need for offline access and the nature of the data. The durable persistence rules seem to fit the usage.\n\n\n"
