  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Preset Organization**\n\nI\'m currently evaluating the most effective way to integrate preset management within the StudioToolTab. I\'m exploring the idea of a dedicated \"PRESETS\" tab, potentially categorized under \"Looks\" using an icon. I\'m also considering whether this should be a tab in the studio dock AND a button in the top bar, or if those are redundant.\n\n\n**Integrating Preset Accessibility**\n\nI\'ve realized that the floating action menu provides optimal accessibility for look management alongside core tools like Wheels and Curves. I\'m now comparing `LutManager.kt` with `PresetDialogs.kt` and `PresetManagerPanel.kt` to understand where preset functionality should reside. I\'m also clarifying the distinction between LUTs, which are RGB value mappings, and user presets, which encompass the entire grading configuration. I\'m checking `StudioToolTab` to see if I can add `PRESETS` to allow users to browse, filter, and apply presets.\n\n\n"
