    thinking: "**Analyzing Kotlin Code**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `GradingStudioScreen.kt`. I\'ve begun collecting `savedPresets` using `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` and have set up state variables for dialog visibility. I\'m keeping track of `showSavePresetDialog` and `showPresetManagerDialog` using `remember` and `mutableStateOf`.\n\n\n**Implementing Preset Functionality**\n\nI\'ve just added the Presets button to the TopAppBar, complete with a badged count, which is a nice touch! Next, I\'m working on passing `savedPresets`, `onApplyPreset`, `onCreatePresetClick`, and `onDeletePreset` parameters into both `StudioDockContainer` (for both landscape and portrait layouts) and `StudioFloatingToolSheet`. Finally, I\'m starting to build out the dialogs, specifically the Save User Preset Dialog, including logic to update dialog visibility, call the `viewModel`, display a toast, and the Preset Manager Modal Dialog.\n\n\n"
