  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Color Science**\n\nI\'m now diving into implementing color science within `SamsungLogColorScience.kt`, specifically for CST, False Color, and Split Screen. Currently, I\'m focusing on the CST design and its accuracy, starting with gamut chromatic adaptation matrices for Rec.709 primaries. I\'m keen on establishing this as a strong foundation.\n\n\n**Calculating Color Gamut Matrices**\n\nI\'ve been calculating the standard conversion matrices to linear Rec.709 from other color spaces, which are essential. I\'ve focused on deriving matrices for DaVinci Wide Gamut and Rec.2020. This involves using the primaries of each color space, including Rec.709, and constructing conversion equations based on their chromaticity coordinates. These matrices are crucial for accurate color transformations.\n\n\n**Deriving Color Space Conversions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on deriving key color space conversion equations. I\'ve formulated the DCI-P3 to Rec.709 matrix, which is vital for maintaining accurate color. Additionally, I\'ve begun to evaluate OETF and EOTF gamma conversions, like those for DaVinci Intermediate and Rec.709. I\'m carefully considering how these conversions impact the overall visual output and trying to ensure they are mathematically sound.\n\n\n"
