    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Enhancement**\n\nI\'ve been digging into the `gradeBitmap` function. Specifically, I\'m focusing on how exposure, brightness, and white balance are handled. I see how each color channel (r, g, b) is scaled by `exposureScale`. Then, the code adjusts brightness if `settings.brightness` is non-zero.\n\n\n**Investigating Saturation & Boost**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in the saturation and color boost components. I\'ve pinpointed the use of luminance (lum) calculations using coefficients (LR, LG, LB). I\'m tracing how the `colorBoost` setting impacts the `boostFactor` and ultimately, how it\'s integrated to selectively enhance each color channel. Then, I see how `satVal` is incorporated as well.\n\n\n**Examining Post-Processing Steps**\n\nNow I\'m looking at the final stages of processing. I\'ve reached the Color Space Transform (CST) node, seeing how `applyColorSpaceTransform` handles the color channels (r, g, b) when enabled. I\'m also examining the False Color exposure metering and how it impacts the image data. Finally, the split-screen comparison, controlled by `settings.splitScreenWipe`, is also taking place.\n\n\n"
