  planner_response {
    response: "### 1. Primary Adjustment Sliders (Resolve Primaries Deck)\nWe have added a dedicated **Primary Adjustment Bars Deck** directly underneath the Lift, Gamma, Gain, and Offset color wheels in the **Primaries** tab:\n\n- **Brightness / Exposure**: `-2.00 EV` to `+2.00 EV` precision gain multiplier.\n- **Contrast**: `0.50` to `1.80` with a neutral `0.43` midtone pivot.\n- **Temperature (WB)**: `-100` (cool blue) to `+100` (warm amber).\n- **Tint**: `-100` (green shift) to `+100` (magenta shift).\n- **Saturation**: `0%` (monochrome) to `200%` (full vibrancy).\n- **Shadows**: Dedicated lift recovery curve that isolates the bottom 25% tonal range.\n- **Highlights**: Dedicated highlight compression that isolates specular rolloff above 75% luminance.\n- **Color Boost (Smart Vibrance)**: Selectively boosts undersaturated areas without oversaturating or clipping skin tones.\n- **Quick Reset Buttons**: Every slider includes an individual reset button to instantly restore its default value, plus a master **\"RESET ALL\"** header action.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Color Space Transform (CST) Final Output Node\nIn DaVinci Resolve Studio, professional colorists grade in an intermediate wide working gamut and place a **Color Space Transform (CST)** on the final node before delivery. We have added the **CST Node** tab and an interactive node graph:\n\n- **Visual Node Graph**: Displays signal flow (`[01 S24 RAW] \342\206\222 [02 WHEELS] \342\206\222 [03 CURVES] \342\206\222 [04 FILM FX] \342\206\222 [05 CST NODE]`) with active status indicator and a one-tap bypass switch.\n- **Input Color Space**:\n  - `DaVinci Wide Gamut (DWG)` *(Default)*\n  - `Samsung S24 Log (BT.2020)`\n  - `ARRI Wide Gamut 4`\n  - `Sony S-Gamut3.Cine`\n  - `Rec.709`\n- **Input Gamma**:\n  - `DaVinci Intermediate` *(Default)*\n  - `Samsung S24 Ultra Log`\n  - `ARRI LogC4`\n  - `Linear`\n- **Output Color Space**:\n  - `Rec.709 (HD / SDR Broadcast Delivery)` *(Default)*\n  - `DCI-P3 (Theatrical Digital Cinema)`\n  - `Rec.2020 (UHD Master)`\n  - `sRGB (Web & Mobile)`\n- **Output Gamma**:\n  - `Gamma 2.4 (Studio Monitor Standard)`\n  - `Rec.709`\n  - `Gamma 2.2 (Standard PC Display)`\n  - `sRGB`\n- **DaVinci Tone Mapping**: Saturation-preserving luminance shoulder compression with an adjustable knee threshold (`0.50` to `0.95`).\n- **Gamut Saturation Compression**: Prevents out-of-gamut color clipping in broadcast delivery.\n- **One-Tap CST Templates**: Quick presets for *DaVinci Wide Gamut \342\206\222 Rec.709*, *Samsung S24 Log \342\206\222 Rec.709*, and *Samsung S24 Log \342\206\222 DCI-P3*.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Additional Resolve Studio Tools Implemented\nTo match DaVinci Resolve Studio\'s grading suite:\n- **False Color Exposure Metering**: Added a one-tap toggle on the video monitor top bar. Maps luminance into industry-standard IRE exposure bands:\n  - *Purple (0\342\200\2232 IRE)*: Crushed black clipping\n  - *Blue (2\342\200\22310 IRE)*: Shadow detail\n  - *Green (38\342\200\22344 IRE)*: 18% Middle Gray card reference\n  - *Pink (48\342\200\22356 IRE)*: Skin tone target exposure\n  - *Yellow (80\342\200\22395 IRE)*: Specular highlight warning\n  - *Red (95\342\200\223100+ IRE)*: Blown clipped highlights\n- **A/B Split Screen Wipe**: Drag or toggle side-by-side comparison between the raw log footage and your active grade.\n\n---\n\n### 4. How to Test and Install on Your Phone\n\nThe project has compiled and the debug APK has been assembled:\n\n#### Option A: Install the APK directly on your Android phone\n1. In the **AI Studio top-right settings/export menu**, select **Export** \342\206\222 **Download APK / Generate APK**.\n2. Alternatively, transfer `app-debug.apk` (built at `app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk`) to your phone via USB or Google Drive.\n3. On your phone, tap the APK file and select **Install** (if prompted, enable *\"Install unknown apps\"* in Settings).\n\n#### Option B: Make the app link public & test via browser\n1. In the top-right corner of Google AI Studio, click the **Share** button.\n2. Toggle the visibility to **Public** or **Anyone with the link**.\n3. Open your **Shared App URL** on your mobile browser to run the streaming interactive emulator directly on your phone:\n   - **Shared URL**: `https://ais-pre-eayknkklreuscrpldkkjex-402014018267.europe-west3.run.app`"
    thinking: "**Analyzing APK Details**\n\nI\'ve determined that the debug APK, `app-debug.apk`, is now fully built and signed, clocking in at 23MB. I\'m starting to analyze the remaining options to reach the Davinci Resolve Studio color grade quality, starting with its features.\n\n\n**Matching Color Grade Features**\n\nI\'ve just added the \"Primary Adjustment Sliders Deck\", now including Brightness/Exposure EV, Contrast, Temperature, Tint, Saturation, Shadows recovery, Highlights compression, and Color Boost. The goal is to fully match DaVinci Resolve Studio. The next stage of comparison will be examining the remaining missing feature sets.\n\n\n**Adding Feature Sets**\n\nI\'m now focusing on critical features for achieving DaVinci Resolve Studio-level color grading. I\'m adding a Color Space Transform (CST) output node, enabling conversions between color spaces, including DaVinci Wide Gamut (DWG) and Samsung S24 Log (BT.2020), with tone mapping. I\'m also adding a False Color Exposure Metering tool and A/B Split Screen Wipe functionality for direct comparisons. These additions are key to replicating the professional workflow.\n\n\n**Implementing Color Transforms**\n\nI\'ve successfully implemented a Color Space Transform (CST) node, crucial for converting DaVinci Wide Gamut (DWG) to Rec.709 with Gamma 2.4/2.2, or Rec.709 OETF. The CST node in `CstNodePanel.kt` utilizes tone mapping for highlight roll-off and gamut saturation compression through `SamsungLogColorScience.kt`. I\'ve also detailed how to access and install the debug APK on a phone via the Shared App URL.\n\n\n"
