  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Bezier Interactions**\n\nI\'ve made progress on handling touch interaction within `MaskingOverlay.kt` for both Elliptical and Rectangular masks. Now, I\'m focusing on designing a fully interactive, Bezier-based masking tool for custom-drawn shapes, which can facilitate localized color adjustments as requested.\n\n\n**Developing Bezier Masking**\n\nI\'m now integrating a `CUSTOM_BEZIER` mask type, with control points defined by a `BezierControlPoint` data class. I\'ve defined the logic for ray casting and distance evaluation for the custom Bezier shapes. The UI component in `MaskingOverlay.kt` is rendering the Bezier path and handles, with active selections displayed.\n\n\n**Implementing Bezier Controls**\n\nI\'ve just added interaction controls for the Bezier mask! Tapping near the perimeter selects a point, which can then be dragged. A delete button is included in the toolbar, and quick toolbar actions for \"Add Point\", \"Reset Shape,\" and \"Close/Open Curve\" are implemented. The controls are located in `PowerWindowControls.kt`. I\'m integrating mask type selection, and adding the Bezier editing toolbar, that includes controls for feathering, inverting, and matte toggling!\n\n\n**Analyzing Fuji Film Styles**\n\nI\'m now diving into replicating Fujifilm film characteristics. I\'m focusing on analyzing the tonal and color biases of various simulations: `FUJI_NOSTALGIC_NEGATIVE`, `FUJI_VELVIA`, `FUJI_PROVIA`, `FUJI_ASTIA`, and `FUJI_ACROS`. I\'m breaking down their key features, like the warm shadows of Nostalgic Negative and the intense greens of Velvia, to inform my implementation. I\'m also considering aspects of film grain.\n\n\n"
