  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying LUT Recipes**\n\nI\'ve got `applyLutPreset` functioning cleanly, calibrated mathematically! My next focus is on verifying what the seven Fujifilm recipe LUTs *should* do. For example, I am specifically looking at FUJI_CLASSIC_CHROME, which shows muted saturation, with deep cyan/navy blues, warmer red/yellow skin tones, and soft highlights.\n\n\n**Analyzing Film Recipe Characteristics**\n\nI\'m now diving into the nuances of each Fujifilm recipe. I have a good grasp of the distinctive characteristics. For Classic Negative, I\'ve noted the high contrast, magenta cast in shadows, cooler highlights, and warm red accents. Nostalgic Negative\'s warm amber tint and Velvia\'s punchy blacks are also clear. I\'m noting the nuances of Provia, Astia, and Acros, now.\n\n\n**Implementing Bezier Curves**\n\nI\'ve defined `BezierControlPoint` and extended `PowerWindowMask` to include a list of `bezierPoints` and an `isClosed` flag. A default 4-point Bezier shape is now available. I\'ve also implemented `evaluateBezierMask` in `SamsungLogColorScience.kt`, which handles discretization, point-in-polygon determination, distance measurement, and smoothstep feathering. Next, I am working on adding interactive Bezier editing in `MaskingOverlay.kt` to allow smooth and intuitive control.\n\n\n**Designing Bezier Interactions**\n\nI\'m now focused on interactive control of Bezier paths. Amber nodes represent anchor points, cyan diamonds are tangent handles. I can drag these for vertex and curve manipulation. A viewport tap adds a point, and a floating toolbar enables quick actions: shape switching, point addition/deletion, path closure, resetting, inverting, and matte toggles. I\'ve also integrated the Bezier control option into the masking options.\n\n\n**Adding Film Simulation Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating realistic color transforms and film grain characteristics for the seven Fujifilm film recipes within `SamsungLogColorScience.kt`. I\'m going to associate each recipe with authentic film grain details. I\'m also adding a filter chip in `LutManager.kt` and starter presets showcasing these looks with matched film grain in `GradePreset.kt`.\n\n\n"
