  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying User Needs**\n\nI\'ve got a solid grasp of the overall project, and I\'m diving deeper into the specific user requirements. I\'m focusing on the functionality of the masking tool, especially its Bezier-based nature and the need for circular, rectangular, and custom shape options. The goal is to accurately interpret the initial ask.\n\n\n**Defining Mask Features**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the mask features. My focus is on implementing Bezier curves for custom shapes, alongside elliptical, rectangular, and linear options. I\'m working through the data structures in `ColorGradeState.kt`, including `MaskType` and the `BezierControlPoint` data class, and I\'m figuring out how best to represent handles for the Bezier curves.\n\n\n**Refining Bezier Implementation**\n\nI\'m leaning towards absolute, normalized coordinates for Bezier control points to simplify drawing and manipulation. This approach makes moving anchors and handles very intuitive. I\'m also proposing a default 4-point diamond shape as a starting point, complete with smooth handles. Finally, I\'m thinking about updating the `PowerWindowMask` data class.\n\n\n**Analyzing Bezier Evaluation**\n\nI\'m now digging into the `evaluateBezierMask` function. My focus is on understanding how closed Bezier loops are processed for the masking tool. I\'m considering using ray casting or winding number algorithms after sampling the spline, and also how to handle feathering. I\'m exploring the logic for determining if a point is inside the mask and how to weight the result based on distance to ensure smooth transitions. I\'m also planning to modify the `PowerWindowMask` data class.\n\n\n**Evaluating Feathering Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on feathering within Bezier masks, focusing on the proposed mathematical formulation. I\'ve confirmed a smooth transition from inside to outside using the formula. I will work on verifying its performance. In parallel, I will update the code with the feather width value.\n\nIn `MaskingOverlay.kt`, I\'ll draw the closed Bezier path on Canvas using `path.cubicTo`. I\'m going to add the dashed feather outline and the anchor points with highlighting for selection. Tangent lines will also need to be drawn for handles.\n\n\n**Implementing User Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user input. Tapping an anchor point selects it, and dragging adjusts the point\'s position and handle relationships. Handle dragging modifies tangents directly. Double-taps will add or reset points. I\'m considering quick toolbar options for adding, deleting, closing, resetting, inverting, and matte viewing.\n\nI\'m also working to integrate the custom Bezier mask into the UI. I will update the shape selector tabs in `PowerWindowOverlay.kt` to include the Bezier option, which displays relevant controls like the point counter badge, and point add/delete/reset functionality. A feather slider will also be added.\n\n\n**Categorizing Simulation Profiles**\n\nI\'m now cataloging the provided simulation profiles based on their characteristics. I\'m grouping them by aesthetic categories: Classic Chrome is documentary-style, Classic Negative offers a unique film look with color shifts, and Nostalgic Negative reflects slide film aesthetics. I can also clearly see the differences between Vivid (Velvia) and Standard (Provia) styles, with Soft (Astia) emphasizing a gentler tone. ACROS is a separate case.\n\n\n**Defining ACROS Implementation**\n\nI\'m now integrating ACROS into the Fujifilm film recipes. I\'m structuring them within `LutCategory.FUJIFILM(\"Fujifilm Film Recipes\")` and adding corresponding presets in `LutPreset`: `FUJI_CLASSIC_CHROME`, `FUJI_CLASSIC_NEGATIVE`, `FUJI_NOSTALGIC_NEGATIVE`, `FUJI_VELVIA`, `FUJI_PROVIA`, `FUJI_ASTIA`, and the distinctive `FUJI_ACROS`. My next task involves refining the color science within `SamsungLogColorScience.kt` for each of the seven presets. This will involve mapping Samsung S24 Log to linear/Rec.709 and then applying film recipe curves, matrix color shifts, and tone responses. I\'ll also add custom color gradients in `LutManager.kt` for each preset. Finally, I will provide a guide to make the app public and downloadable in the Google Play Store.\n\n\n"
