    thinking: "**Analyzing Color Science Logic**\n\nI\'ve just updated my notes following an examination of `ColorGradeState.kt`. My focus has now shifted to `SamsungLogColorScience.kt`. The next step is to implement the `evaluateBezierMask` function, specifically addressing the `MaskType.CUSTOM_BEZ` case.\n\n\n**Implementing Bezier Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation of `evaluateBezierMask`, specifically for `MaskType.CUSTOM_BEZ`. My current focus is on understanding and translating the Bezier curve math. I\'ve broken down the Bezier curve calculation into its components and am working on how to sample the curves into linear segments. I\'m also planning the ray casting algorithm to determine if a point lies within the generated polygon.\n\n\n**Calculating Polygon Distance**\n\nI\'ve been working on computing the distance to the polygon boundary, specifically focusing on how to determine the shortest distance from a point (u, v) to each segment (pa, pb). I\'m implementing the `distToSegmentSq` function and need to calculate the signed distance, taking into account whether a point is inside or outside the polygon. I will also incorporate feathering width to smooth the transition, and apply Hermite smoothstep to weight.\n\n\n**Refining Polygon Distance Logic**\n\nI\'ve refined the polygon distance logic, addressing the smoothing. I\'m focusing on ensuring a continuous, fast, and mathematically sound approach. The weight calculation is now tied to whether the point lies inside or outside the polygon and the integration of a smoothstep function to control feathering. I\'m satisfied with the current progress.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Adding LUT Preset Cases**\n\nI am now adding the Fujifilm recipe presets to `applyLutPreset`. I\'ve begun with Classic Chrome, targeting its characteristic muted saturation, high contrast, cyan-tinted skies, and warm skin tones. I\'m going through the other Fujifilm presets, focusing on their unique characteristics, like the Superia 400 emulation of Classic Negative and Nostalgic Negative\'s amber cast.\n\n\n"
