  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Bezier Gestures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the system handles gestures specifically when the `mask.type` is set to `MaskType.CUSTOM_BEZIER`. It\'s clear there\'s a need to differentiate the different drag targets, with the `bezierDragTarget` enum crucial here: NONE, ANCHOR, HANDLE_IN, and HANDLE_OUT. This distinction is vital for accurate bezier curve manipulation during interactions.\n\n\n**Defining Drag Targets**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out the logic for `CUSTOM_BEZIER` gesture handling, specifically how we determine the drag target. Initial analysis focuses on distance checks: identifying the closest anchor point within a `hitRadius`, then handling `handleIn` and `handleOut` points if within range. I\'m considering using an enum `BezierDragTarget` to manage interactions, differentiating between `ANCHOR`, `HANDLE_IN`, `HANDLE_OUT`, and `WHOLE_SHAPE` drags. The bounds are constrained with `coerceIn`.\n\n\n"
