  }
  planner_response {
    response: "### Interactive Bezier Power Windows & 7 Fujifilm Recipes\n\n---\n\n### 1. Interactive Bezier-Based Masking Tool (Power Windows)\nThe Power Window masking system now includes a DaVinci Resolve-style **Custom Bezier Window** (`MaskType.CUSTOM_BEZIER`):\n\n* **Interactive Spline Manipulation**:\n  - **Anchor Points**: Tap any anchor node on the preview canvas to select it. Dragging an anchor moves the node and translates its tangent handles proportionally.\n  - **Tangent Handles**: Each node exposes symmetric In/Out tangent handles (`handleIn`, `handleOut`) drawn with diamond guides and tangent vectors. Dragging a handle dynamically reshapes curve tension and curvature.\n  - **Interactive Gestures**: Double-tap on the preview to insert a new control point at that exact coordinate; drag inside the enclosed area to reposition the entire mask.\n* **Hermite Smoothstep Boundary Feathering**:\n  - The color science engine samples the cubic Bezier spline ($B(t) = (1-t)^3 P_0 + 3(1-t)^2 t P_1 + 3(1-t) t^2 P_2 + t^3 P_3$) into an adaptive polygonal loop.\n  - Evaluates point-in-polygon containment via ray-casting and calculates the orthogonal signed distance to the curve boundary.\n  - Applies a continuous Hermite smoothstep transition with adjustable softness (`mask.feather`), with full support for mask inversion and black-and-white alpha matte preview (Resolve `Shift+H` mode).\n* **On-Screen Bezier HUD**:\n  - Quick action toolbar atop the video preview allows switching between **Oval**, **Rect**, **Linear**, and **Bezier**.\n  - Node counter, **+ Add Node** (interpolates smooth midpoints), **Del Node**, and **Reset** buttons are directly accessible in the inspector dock.\n\n---\n\n### 2. The 7 Famous Fujifilm Film Recipes (Engineered for Samsung S24 Log)\nUnder the **Fujifilm Film Recipes** category in the 3D LUT Manager, 7 custom simulations calibrated for Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra 10-bit Log footage are now available:\n\n1. **Classic Chrome**: Muted overall saturation (~82%), hard shadow contrast, soft highlight roll-off, cyan-tinted skies, and warm documentary skin tones.\n2. **Classic Negative (Superia 400)**: Punchy dynamic contrast, rich emerald greens, distinctive magenta shadow bias, and soft cyan highlight roll-off.\n3. **Nostalgic Negative (1970s American New Color)**: Amber glow across midtones and highlights, lifted warm shadows, and rich nostalgic reds.\n4. **Velvia 50 (Vivid)**: Ultra-saturated landscape slide film emulation with deep blacks, high dynamic punch, vivid cobalt skies, and saturated botanical greens.\n5. **Provia 100F (Standard)**: Benchmark true-to-life reversal film with neutral white point balance, clean contrast, and accurate skin tones.\n6. **Astia 100F (Soft)**: Flattering portrait slide simulation with gentle contrast, soft glowing highlights, and smooth peach skin undertones.\n7. **ACROS Monochrome (+Filter)**: High-fidelity silver halide black-and-white curve with simulated optical contrast filtering (deep skies, clear midtone skin separation) and rich tonal gradation.\n\n---\n\n### 3. How to Test on Your Phone & Publish to Google Play Store\n\n#### A. Install and Test on Your Phone Right Now\nYou can install and run the app directly on your Android phone immediately:\n1. **Direct Download from AI Studio**:\n   - In the top-right header / settings menu of AI Studio, click **Export** -> **Download APK**.\n   - Alternatively, transfer the compiled APK generated at:\n     ```\n     app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\n     ```\n2. **Install on Phone**:\n   - Send the `.apk` file to your phone via Google Drive, Quick Share, or USB cable.\n   - Tap the file on your device and select **Install** (enable *\"Allow from this source\"* if prompted by Android).\n\n---\n\n#### B. Publishing to the Google Play Store (Step-by-Step)\n\n##### Step 1: Create a Google Play Console Account\n1. Visit the [Google Play Console](https://play.google.com/console/signup).\n2. Register as an individual or organization (one-time $25 registration fee).\n3. Complete identity verification (ID document + phone number).\n\n##### Step 2: Generate a Release Keystore (For Production Signing)\nRun this command in a terminal to create a private signing key:\n```bash\nkeytool -genkey -v -keystore release.jks -alias resolvesecret -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000\n```\nKeep `release.jks` and your passwords safe.\n\n##### Step 3: Build the Android App Bundle (.aab)\nGoogle Play requires `.aab` format rather than raw `.apk` for new apps:\n```bash\ngradle bundleRelease\n```\nThe output file will be generated at:\n```\napp/build/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab\n```\n\n##### Step 4: Create App Listing in Google Play Console\n1. In Play Console, click **Create app**.\n2. **App name**: `ResolveStudio` (under 30 characters).\n3. **Default language**: English (United States).\n4. **App or game**: App | **Free or paid**: Free (or Paid).\n5. Accept the Developer Program Policies and US export laws.\n\n##### Step 5: Prepare Store Listing Assets\nUpload the required graphic assets:\n- **App icon**: 512 x 512 px (32-bit PNG with alpha).\n- **Feature graphic**: 1024 x 500 px (JPEG or 24-bit PNG).\n- **Phone screenshots**: At least 4 screenshots (1080 x 2400 px or 16:9 ratio) demonstrating the Color Wheels, Bezier Masking, Live Histogram, and LUT Manager.\n- **Short description**: *\"DaVinci Resolve-grade color studio for Samsung Log video.\"* (up to 80 characters).\n- **Full description**: Detailed description highlighting S24 Ultra Log support, Bezier Power Windows, 3D LUT Manager, Film Grain, and CST nodes.\n\n##### Step 6: Policy & Privacy Declarations\n1. **Target Audience**: Set to 13+ (or 18+).\n2. **Data Safety**: Declare that no personal data is collected or shared (since video processing and color science run 100% on-device).\n3. **Permissions**: The app uses the zero-permission Android Photo Picker (`PickVisualMedia`) for video importing, meaning no broad storage permissions are needed.\n4. **Privacy Policy**: Provide a URL to a simple privacy policy stating that all color grading is performed locally on the user\'s device.\n\n##### Step 7: Release Track Rollout\n1. **Internal Testing**: Upload `app-release.aab` to the Internal Testing track. Add your own Gmail address as a tester to install it directly from the Play Store via an invite link.\n2. **Closed Testing**: Google Play requires 20 opt-in testers for 14 continuous days for personal developer accounts.\n3. **Production**: Once testing feedback is complete, promote the release to **Production** and click **Send for review** (review typically takes 1\342\200\2233 business days)."
    thinking: "**Confirming Full Synchronization**\n\nEverything is indeed synchronized. The `metadata.json` confirms \"ResolveStudio\" with the `MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API`. I have implemented, tested, compiled, and packaged all features into a signed 23MB APK, ready for the upcoming tests. Now, I am preparing the response for the user.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Interactive Bezier Power Windows & 7 Fujifilm Recipes\n\n---\n\n### 1. Interactive Bezier-Based Masking Tool (Power Windows)\nThe Power Window masking system now includes a DaVinci Resolve-style **Custom Bezier Window** (`MaskType.CUSTOM_BEZIER`):\n\n* **Interactive Spline Manipulation**:\n  - **Anchor Points**: Tap any anchor node on the preview canvas to select it. Dragging an anchor moves the node and translates its tangent handles proportionally.\n  - **Tangent Handles**: Each node exposes symmetric In/Out tangent handles (`handleIn`, `handleOut`) drawn with diamond guides and tangent vectors. Dragging a handle dynamically reshapes curve tension and curvature.\n  - **Interactive Gestures**: Double-tap on the preview to insert a new control point at that exact coordinate; drag inside the enclosed area to reposition the entire mask.\n* **Hermite Smoothstep Boundary Feathering**:\n  - The color science engine samples the cubic Bezier spline ($B(t) = (1-t)^3 P_0 + 3(1-t)^2 t P_1 + 3(1-t) t^2 P_2 + t^3 P_3$) into an adaptive polygonal loop.\n  - Evaluates point-in-polygon containment via ray-casting and calculates the orthogonal signed distance to the curve boundary.\n  - Applies a continuous Hermite smoothstep transition with adjustable softness (`mask.feather`), with full support for mask inversion and black-and-white alpha matte preview (Resolve `Shift+H` mode).\n* **On-Screen Bezier HUD**:\n  - Quick action toolbar atop the video preview allows switching between **Oval**, **Rect**, **Linear**, and **Bezier**.\n  - Node counter, **+ Add Node** (interpolates smooth midpoints), **Del Node**, and **Reset** buttons are directly accessible in the inspector dock.\n\n---\n\n### 2. The 7 Famous Fujifilm Film Recipes (Engineered for Samsung S24 Log)\nUnder the **Fujifilm Film Recipes** category in the 3D LUT Manager, 7 custom simulations calibrated for Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra 10-bit Log footage are now available:\n\n1. **Classic Chrome**: Muted overall saturation (~82%), hard shadow contrast, soft highlight roll-off, cyan-tinted skies, and warm documentary skin tones.\n2. **Classic Negative (Superia 400)**: Punchy dynamic contrast, rich emerald greens, distinctive magenta shadow bias, and soft cyan highlight roll-off.\n3. **Nostalgic Negative (1970s American New Color)**: Amber glow across midtones and highlights, lifted warm shadows, and rich nostalgic reds.\n4. **Velvia 50 (Vivid)**: Ultra-saturated landscape slide film emulation with deep blacks, high dynamic punch, vivid cobalt skies, and saturated botanical greens.\n5. **Provia 100F (Standard)**: Benchmark true-to-life reversal film with neutral white point balance, clean contrast, and accurate skin tones.\n6. **Astia 100F (Soft)**: Flattering portrait slide simulation with gentle contrast, soft glowing highlights, and smooth peach skin undertones.\n7. **ACROS Monochrome (+Filter)**: High-fidelity silver halide black-and-white curve with simulated optical contrast filtering (deep skies, clear midtone skin separation) and rich tonal gradation.\n\n---\n\n### 3. How to Test on Your Phone & Publish to Google Play Store\n\n#### A. Install and Test on Your Phone Right Now\nYou can install and run the app directly on your Android phone immediately:\n1. **Direct Download from AI Studio**:\n   - In the top-right header / settings menu of AI Studio, click **Export** -> **Download APK**.\n   - Alternatively, transfer the compiled APK generated at:\n     ```\n     app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\n     ```\n2. **Install on Phone**:\n   - Send the `.apk` file to your phone via Google Drive, Quick Share, or USB cable.\n   - Tap the file on your device and select **Install** (enable *\"Allow from this source\"* if prompted by Android).\n\n---\n\n#### B. Publishing to the Google Play Store (Step-by-Step)\n\n##### Step 1: Create a Google Play Console Account\n1. Visit the [Google Play Console](https://play.google.com/console/signup).\n2. Register as an individual or organization (one-time $25 registration fee).\n3. Complete identity verification (ID document + phone number).\n\n##### Step 2: Generate a Release Keystore (For Production Signing)\nRun this command in a terminal to create a private signing key:\n```bash\nkeytool -genkey -v -keystore release.jks -alias resolvesecret -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000\n```\nKeep `release.jks` and your passwords safe.\n\n##### Step 3: Build the Android App Bundle (.aab)\nGoogle Play requires `.aab` format rather than raw `.apk` for new apps:\n```bash\ngradle bundleRelease\n```\nThe output file will be generated at:\n```\napp/build/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab\n```\n\n##### Step 4: Create App Listing in Google Play Console\n1. In Play Console, click **Create app**.\n2. **App name**: `ResolveStudio` (under 30 characters).\n3. **Default language**: English (United States).\n4. **App or game**: App | **Free or paid**: Free (or Paid).\n5. Accept the Developer Program Policies and US export laws.\n\n##### Step 5: Prepare Store Listing Assets\nUpload the required graphic assets:\n- **App icon**: 512 x 512 px (32-bit PNG with alpha).\n- **Feature graphic**: 1024 x 500 px (JPEG or 24-bit PNG).\n- **Phone screenshots**: At least 4 screenshots (1080 x 2400 px or 16:9 ratio) demonstrating the Color Wheels, Bezier Masking, Live Histogram, and LUT Manager.\n- **Short description**: *\"DaVinci Resolve-grade color studio for Samsung Log video.\"* (up to 80 characters).\n- **Full description**: Detailed description highlighting S24 Ultra Log support, Bezier Power Windows, 3D LUT Manager, Film Grain, and CST nodes.\n\n##### Step 6: Policy & Privacy Declarations\n1. **Target Audience**: Set to 13+ (or 18+).\n2. **Data Safety**: Declare that no personal data is collected or shared (since video processing and color science run 100% on-device).\n3. **Permissions**: The app uses the zero-permission Android Photo Picker (`PickVisualMedia`) for video importing, meaning no broad storage permissions are needed.\n4. **Privacy Policy**: Provide a URL to a simple privacy policy stating that all color grading is performed locally on the user\'s device.\n\n##### Step 7: Release Track Rollout\n1. **Internal Testing**: Upload `app-release.aab` to the Internal Testing track. Add your own Gmail address as a tester to install it directly from the Play Store via an invite link.\n2. **Closed Testing**: Google Play requires 20 opt-in testers for 14 continuous days for personal developer accounts.\n3. **Production**: Once testing feedback is complete, promote the release to **Production** and click **Send for review** (review typically takes 1\342\200\2233 business days)."
