  planner_response {
    response: "When working outside of AI Studio (in **Antigravity** or a local IDE), you don\'t have the cloud \"Publish\" button, but you have **two straightforward workflows** to update and test the app on your phone:\n\n---\n\n### Option 1: Direct APK Build (Fastest for testing)\n\nWhenever you make code changes in Antigravity, you can build an updated APK in seconds right from the terminal:\n\n1. **Build the updated APK in Antigravity terminal**:\n   ```bash\n   ./gradlew assembleDebug\n   ```\n   *(If you are on Windows PowerShell: `.\\gradlew.bat assembleDebug`)*\n\n2. **Locate the new APK**:\n   Your updated app will be in:\n   ```\n   app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\n   ```\n\n3. **Install it on your phone**:\n   * **Via USB (Instant with ADB)**:\n     If your phone is plugged in with USB debugging enabled:\n     ```bash\n     adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\n     ```\n     The `-r` flag replaces the existing app while keeping all your custom saved presets and settings.\n   * **Or Wireless**:\n     Transfer `app-debug.apk` to your phone via Quick Share, Google Drive, or Telegram and tap **Update**.\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: The GitHub $\\rightarrow$ AI Studio \"Publish\" Loop (If you want Google Play updates)\n\nIf you prefer having the update delivered through the **Google Play Store** on your phone without manually copying APK files:\n\n1. **Commit and push from Antigravity**:\n   ```bash\n   git add .\n   git commit -m \"New color grading updates\"\n   git push origin main\n   ```\n2. **Open the AI Studio tab**:\n   * Pull the latest commit from your GitHub repo.\n3. **Click \"Publish\"**:\n   * AI Studio will compile the latest GitHub code and push the update straight to your Google Play library on your phone.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Recommendation\n* For **rapid day-to-day coding in Antigravity**: Use **Option 1** (`./gradlew assembleDebug` or `adb install -r`) \342\200\224 it takes under 10 seconds.\n* When you want a **milestone release installed through Google Play**: Use **Option 2** (Git push $\\rightarrow$ AI Studio Publish)."
    thinking: "**Exploring Antigravity Workflow**\n\nI\'m currently figuring out the best workflow for updating projects within Antigravity, specifically since it lacks a \"publish\" button. I\'m trying to determine how to integrate my existing work, exported from a different IDE, effectively, and understand how the update process is designed within this environment.\n\n\n**Defining Update Procedures**\n\nI\'ve determined there are three primary methods for updating the app on my phone when working outside AI Studio. The first involves building the APK directly in the Antigravity terminal and installing it, the fastest and most direct approach. The second option focuses on pushing updates through Git, and the third remains the subject of my thoughts.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "When working outside of AI Studio (in **Antigravity** or a local IDE), you don\'t have the cloud \"Publish\" button, but you have **two straightforward workflows** to update and test the app on your phone:\n\n---\n\n### Option 1: Direct APK Build (Fastest for testing)\n\nWhenever you make code changes in Antigravity, you can build an updated APK in seconds right from the terminal:\n\n1. **Build the updated APK in Antigravity terminal**:\n   ```bash\n   ./gradlew assembleDebug\n   ```\n   *(If you are on Windows PowerShell: `.\\gradlew.bat assembleDebug`)*\n\n2. **Locate the new APK**:\n   Your updated app will be in:\n   ```\n   app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\n   ```\n\n3. **Install it on your phone**:\n   * **Via USB (Instant with ADB)**:\n     If your phone is plugged in with USB debugging enabled:\n     ```bash\n     adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\n     ```\n     The `-r` flag replaces the existing app while keeping all your custom saved presets and settings.\n   * **Or Wireless**:\n     Transfer `app-debug.apk` to your phone via Quick Share, Google Drive, or Telegram and tap **Update**.\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: The GitHub $\\rightarrow$ AI Studio \"Publish\" Loop (If you want Google Play updates)\n\nIf you prefer having the update delivered through the **Google Play Store** on your phone without manually copying APK files:\n\n1. **Commit and push from Antigravity**:\n   ```bash\n   git add .\n   git commit -m \"New color grading updates\"\n   git push origin main\n   ```\n2. **Open the AI Studio tab**:\n   * Pull the latest commit from your GitHub repo.\n3. **Click \"Publish\"**:\n   * AI Studio will compile the latest GitHub code and push the update straight to your Google Play library on your phone.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Recommendation\n* For **rapid day-to-day coding in Antigravity**: Use **Option 1** (`./gradlew assembleDebug` or `adb install -r`) \342\200\224 it takes under 10 seconds.\n* When you want a **milestone release installed through Google Play**: Use **Option 2** (Git push $\\rightarrow$ AI Studio Publish)."
