  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Calculating Action Widths**\n\nI\'ve been calculating the total width of the action buttons within the specified lines. So far, I\'ve identified several elements: Undo, Redo, History, Presets, Scene selector, Dock toggle, and Reset grade, each using 32dp. Additionally, there\'s an Export button, estimated at around 70dp. I\'m summing these to determine the overall space they require.\n\n\n**Refining UI Component Spacing**\n\nI\'ve just realized the severe space constraints on smaller screens. With roughly 300dp occupied by action buttons, the title has severely limited space. The original \"RESOLVE STUDIO\" text was wrapping awkwardly. I\'m moving forward with a redesigned top header to resolve this by using a unified, non-wrapping title string, a sleek icon, and a \"S24 LOG\" pill badge for concise information.\n\n\n**Optimizing Mobile Action Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on mobile action layouts to maximize the visual clarity. I\'m prioritizing the most frequent actions directly: Undo, Redo, and Export. The studio options will live in a dropdown on compact screens. On wider screens, more buttons may show directly. This keeps the header ultra-clean on phones, ensuring ample space for the title \"RESOLVE STUDIO,\" which will never wrap. I also thought about keeping the **Presets** button.\n\n\n"
