  planner_response {
    response: "### Header Fix & Layout Improvements\n\n#### What caused the \"st ud\" issue:\n1. **Title text wrapping**: Previously, `\"RESOLVE\"` and `\"STUDIO\"` were rendered as two separate `Text` composables. When horizontal screen space was constricted on mobile, `\"STUDIO\"` was wrapped across lines as `\"ST\"` and `\"UD\"`.\n2. **Action button crowding**: The top bar previously contained 7 separate action icon buttons side-by-side (Undo, Redo, History, Presets, Scenes, Dock Mode, Reset Grade, Export), consuming over 300dp of width. On mobile viewports (360dp\342\200\223412dp), this squeezed the title area down to under 80dp.\n\n#### Improvements Made:\n* **Single Non-Wrapping Title**:\n  - Unified the title into a single `buildAnnotatedString` where `\"RESOLVE\"` (in primary white) and `\"STUDIO\"` (in Resolve amber) are locked together with `maxLines = 1` and `softWrap = false`. It can never break across multiple lines or misalign.\n  - Added a color tuner/director emblem (`Icons.Default.Tune`) and a compact `\"S24 LOG\"` pill badge with border framing.\n* **Streamlined Mobile Actions**:\n  - Kept primary instant actions one tap away: **Undo**, **Redo**, **Scene Selector**, and **Export**.\n  - Grouped secondary management utilities (Look Presets Browser, History Stack, Dock Pinning, and Reset Grade) into a dedicated **Studio More Options** menu (`\342\213\256` icon).\n  - The title now has ample breathing room (>180dp) on any device screen.\n\n---\n\n### Why `app/build/outputs/apk/debug/` wasn\'t in your exported folder\n\nIn Android Gradle projects, all `build/` folders are **git-ignored** (`.gitignore`) by standard convention so that heavy binaries (20MB+ APKs) are not stored in Git history. \n\nWhen you export the project or clone from GitHub to Antigravity, the `build/` directory does not exist initially.\n\nTo create it and produce your APK in Antigravity:\n1. Open the terminal in Antigravity.\n2. Run:\n   ```bash\n   ./gradlew assembleDebug\n   ```\n   *(On Windows PowerShell: `.\\gradlew.bat assembleDebug`)*\n3. As soon as Gradle completes the build, the folder and file will appear at:\n   ```\n   app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\n   ```"
    thinking: "**Uncovering Git Ignorance**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the reason for the user\'s missing APK. The culprit? Good old `.gitignore`! It seems the standard Android project setup and typical `.gitignore` configuration specifically exclude the entire `build/` directory, including `app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk`. This exclusion is the root cause of the missing file.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Header Fix & Layout Improvements\n\n#### What caused the \"st ud\" issue:\n1. **Title text wrapping**: Previously, `\"RESOLVE\"` and `\"STUDIO\"` were rendered as two separate `Text` composables. When horizontal screen space was constricted on mobile, `\"STUDIO\"` was wrapped across lines as `\"ST\"` and `\"UD\"`.\n2. **Action button crowding**: The top bar previously contained 7 separate action icon buttons side-by-side (Undo, Redo, History, Presets, Scenes, Dock Mode, Reset Grade, Export), consuming over 300dp of width. On mobile viewports (360dp\342\200\223412dp), this squeezed the title area down to under 80dp.\n\n#### Improvements Made:\n* **Single Non-Wrapping Title**:\n  - Unified the title into a single `buildAnnotatedString` where `\"RESOLVE\"` (in primary white) and `\"STUDIO\"` (in Resolve amber) are locked together with `maxLines = 1` and `softWrap = false`. It can never break across multiple lines or misalign.\n  - Added a color tuner/director emblem (`Icons.Default.Tune`) and a compact `\"S24 LOG\"` pill badge with border framing.\n* **Streamlined Mobile Actions**:\n  - Kept primary instant actions one tap away: **Undo**, **Redo**, **Scene Selector**, and **Export**.\n  - Grouped secondary management utilities (Look Presets Browser, History Stack, Dock Pinning, and Reset Grade) into a dedicated **Studio More Options** menu (`\342\213\256` icon).\n  - The title now has ample breathing room (>180dp) on any device screen.\n\n---\n\n### Why `app/build/outputs/apk/debug/` wasn\'t in your exported folder\n\nIn Android Gradle projects, all `build/` folders are **git-ignored** (`.gitignore`) by standard convention so that heavy binaries (20MB+ APKs) are not stored in Git history. \n\nWhen you export the project or clone from GitHub to Antigravity, the `build/` directory does not exist initially.\n\nTo create it and produce your APK in Antigravity:\n1. Open the terminal in Antigravity.\n2. Run:\n   ```bash\n   ./gradlew assembleDebug\n   ```\n   *(On Windows PowerShell: `.\\gradlew.bat assembleDebug`)*\n3. As soon as Gradle completes the build, the folder and file will appear at:\n   ```\n   app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk\n   ```"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 616530252
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\306\n\n\303\n\001i\024}\023\276\267\"\211\240\255k\313H\037\200\034\277\210m\031U\251\320[\330\364e\003\2775\241\266&}y\rd\253\320\240>\305\226,\354\235|X\310\252\3535\001s\306\021\224*\334\344\005\031$\334\275\366\r\351\246\271I\334\004W\211Q\365\200\253\'\2212\222#\336\216\367\356C\215\243\371\3071G\373\t\336\370\356\000\320J[\354\314\353\032\\H\003\251\224\272\236AZ\316\210\026(!\267f\201)Y/<\002\262NU\016\235\224\363\240\307\343Q;\232|\030\376O\024\260\263)\310\305/\254c\237\177\361\306\373\337\274Rns\035~\217\2569:\332\237\344\"\306\343\222t\003\350\204\214\265\017\330+\r\342&\005m\271;\003\304\363\216\247/\264N \215\343JIA\306\fR\3679\340\210/\243\222\260\035\252?N>^\rf3l1\001\305\371/S\a\2535\256\233<\272>\f\177j<g@\343\255\214\213k\274|\255c 8\021D^\327\253\206\322\245\302$.\212\275\251B\264\026K\354\2464\353\354\2777\177N6P\201]\t\271r\234\234q!\375\273\334\307Lo\261%4u8?\331\220O2O\3212\263\377*\224\334\220\272\336dL\302Z\031\323\311,\260\302F\331\247X\227\240\016\000\204h\032Mv\355\377\024\305\036%\000\275S\301Uh\362\367Uj\262\260\254]\265\217\273\262\264\267\267\024\331\251\250\304\375\240Z\222~\022\372\310a\221\23761s\260\215\214\021i\337\367\333\342\344\001\032\323\vp\021\202\252)\350c\220\270\304\242@T=\340\264n.Ct`\372m\361\360@\b\254\276\376U\337\235k ,\270R\322\235\033dD\312\350.\275\363WT@\\\317=\2265\355+\262]\236D\326h$S\255\340\v\335\207\031\262\032\031\245?\262\230z\304\024\241x\311a\3738A\2255\313\215\237O]\227\205\332\372<\017_\036\222Y\317\t\317YE\322\303\255\030@\r\262\220\312\224d2\215H\'o\375\272q\315\234\3013\313\363\275\253\356\2278$\256\266\357g!\373\251\302\324\314\311hQ\361\265OT(\3659|S\302\201\255\036^\362\341\233\347\352n\2143\360\311\034\316Cj\213%\226\334Um\241*\310\003\346\355\020l\233O\036\222W\275R\261\212\335\201[\016\303gz\346\247i\326\213\003\355\353\3549QJ]\230\364\327TW\2339\217\226\n\233\316J8\204\274\227\266\205\3440\343e\263VK\025`7z\021\254\334\242\376\031\207h\360\313\314%\020\fY\t\303