  planner_response {
    response: "### Real-Time Histogram Scope Overlay Implemented\n\nA cinema-grade **Real-Time Histogram Scope Overlay** (`RealtimeHistogramOverlay.kt`) has been integrated directly into the video viewport to help you visualize the luminance and color channel distribution of your 4K Log footage as you grade.\n\n---\n\n### Key Capabilities\n\n1. **Direct Video Viewport HUD (Monitor Overlay)**:\n   - Sits in the top corner of the video preview window as a translucent dark glass HUD, similar to on-camera monitors (Atomos/SmallHD) and DaVinci Resolve viewer scopes.\n   - Can be toggled on/off instantly using the **Equalizer button** (`testTag(\"histogram_overlay_toggle\")`) in the video header bar, or from the top-bar **Studio More Options** menu (`\342\213\256`).\n\n2. **256-Bin Real-Time Luminance & RGB Channel Graph**:\n   - **`ALL` (Combined Mode)**: Renders the master white luminance envelope layered over subtle red, green, and blue channel distributions.\n   - **`LUM` (Luma Only)**: High-contrast monochrome luminance silhouette with vertical fall-off gradient.\n   - **`RGB` (RGB Parade Overlay)**: Isolated Red, Green, and Blue channel contours.\n   - Tap the mode pill (`ALL` / `LUM` / `RGB`) to switch modes on the fly.\n\n3. **IRE Reference Graticule**:\n   - **0% IRE**: Shadow floor line.\n   - **18% IRE**: Middle-gray dashed reference target for balancing Log exposure.\n   - **50% & 75% IRE**: Midtones and Caucasian skin-tone highlight reference marks.\n   - **100% IRE**: Specular highlight ceiling.\n\n4. **Live Clipping & Dynamic Range Telemetry**:\n   - **Exposure Index**: Shows real-time average scene luminance percentage (`EXP XX%`).\n   - **Shadow Crush Warning**: Alerts in red when black levels fall below 1% IRE.\n   - **Highlight Blowout Alert**: Alerts in red when highlights exceed 99% IRE.\n   - Displays `DYNAMIC RANGE OK` in green when the signal is within legal broadcast limits.\n\n5. **Flat Log vs Graded Rec.709 A/B Comparison (`[RAW]` / `[REC]`)**:\n   - Tap the `[RAW]` / `[REC]` tag in the footer of the histogram HUD to toggle between inspecting the flat Samsung S24 Log dynamic range distribution and the contrast-expanded Rec.709 graded curve.\n\n6. **Compact & Expanded Viewports**:\n   - Tap the expand/contract icon in the scope header to switch between a compact $170\\times95\\text{ dp}$ corner PIP and an expanded $250\\times140\\text{ dp}$ detailed diagnostic view."
    thinking: "**Defining the Overview**\n\nI\'ve successfully built the necessary components! My focus has shifted towards crafting a clear and concise user overview. I\'m starting by outlining the \"what\" \342\200\223 it\'s a Cinema monitor HUD overlay for the video viewport. Next, I plan to detail the \"how\" it functions.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Real-Time Histogram Scope Overlay Implemented\n\nA cinema-grade **Real-Time Histogram Scope Overlay** (`RealtimeHistogramOverlay.kt`) has been integrated directly into the video viewport to help you visualize the luminance and color channel distribution of your 4K Log footage as you grade.\n\n---\n\n### Key Capabilities\n\n1. **Direct Video Viewport HUD (Monitor Overlay)**:\n   - Sits in the top corner of the video preview window as a translucent dark glass HUD, similar to on-camera monitors (Atomos/SmallHD) and DaVinci Resolve viewer scopes.\n   - Can be toggled on/off instantly using the **Equalizer button** (`testTag(\"histogram_overlay_toggle\")`) in the video header bar, or from the top-bar **Studio More Options** menu (`\342\213\256`).\n\n2. **256-Bin Real-Time Luminance & RGB Channel Graph**:\n   - **`ALL` (Combined Mode)**: Renders the master white luminance envelope layered over subtle red, green, and blue channel distributions.\n   - **`LUM` (Luma Only)**: High-contrast monochrome luminance silhouette with vertical fall-off gradient.\n   - **`RGB` (RGB Parade Overlay)**: Isolated Red, Green, and Blue channel contours.\n   - Tap the mode pill (`ALL` / `LUM` / `RGB`) to switch modes on the fly.\n\n3. **IRE Reference Graticule**:\n   - **0% IRE**: Shadow floor line.\n   - **18% IRE**: Middle-gray dashed reference target for balancing Log exposure.\n   - **50% & 75% IRE**: Midtones and Caucasian skin-tone highlight reference marks.\n   - **100% IRE**: Specular highlight ceiling.\n\n4. **Live Clipping & Dynamic Range Telemetry**:\n   - **Exposure Index**: Shows real-time average scene luminance percentage (`EXP XX%`).\n   - **Shadow Crush Warning**: Alerts in red when black levels fall below 1% IRE.\n   - **Highlight Blowout Alert**: Alerts in red when highlights exceed 99% IRE.\n   - Displays `DYNAMIC RANGE OK` in green when the signal is within legal broadcast limits.\n\n5. **Flat Log vs Graded Rec.709 A/B Comparison (`[RAW]` / `[REC]`)**:\n   - Tap the `[RAW]` / `[REC]` tag in the footer of the histogram HUD to toggle between inspecting the flat Samsung S24 Log dynamic range distribution and the contrast-expanded Rec.709 graded curve.\n\n6. **Compact & Expanded Viewports**:\n   - Tap the expand/contract icon in the scope header to switch between a compact $170\\times95\\text{ dp}$ corner PIP and an expanded $250\\times140\\text{ dp}$ detailed diagnostic view."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 976440593
    }
