  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Color Wheel Interactivity**\n\nI\'ve made significant progress with `ColorWheel.kt`. Currently, it boasts Lift, Gamma, Gain, and Offset controls, along with polar hue/saturation calculations, a fine-tune mode, reset functionality, and a Luminance slider. The next logical step is to implement touch interaction, specifically direct tapping on the color wheel to move the reticle puck accordingly.\n\n\n**Implementing Touch Interaction**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated touch interaction within the color wheel. Besides the existing drag functionality, I\'ve incorporated `detectTapGestures` to allow direct tapping on the wheel, enabling precise hue and saturation adjustments. Double-tapping the wheel resets the position to the center. I\'m leveraging `pointerInput` and calculating the tapped offset relative to the wheel\'s radius to map tap coordinates to the appropriate hue and saturation values.\n\n\n"
