  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing ScopesView Canvas**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `ScopesView.kt` file, specifically the vectorscope canvas, and it\'s already implemented with some key elements. These include the polar grid, central crosshairs, a skin tone indicator, and target color boxes. The 75% and 100% legal limit rings are present.\n\n\n**Implementing On-Screen Overlays**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the on-screen scope overlay switcher. The goal is to provide users with the ability to toggle between Histogram and Vectorscope overlays directly on the video. I\'m exploring the `VideoPlayerView` for this functionality, envisioning a switcher for either scope display or a unified RealtimeScopeOverlay. This borrows from features found on professional cinema field monitors. The option to switch directly to the Vectorscope overlay is the new addition.\n\n\n"
