  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 3
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User Requests**:\n  1. *Interactive Primary Color Wheels (Lift, Gamma, Gain)*: Enhance touch-based adjustments for precise color grading control. (Support both direct tap-to-hue/sat positioning and precision drag gestures).\n  2. *Vectorscope*: Implement interactive Vectorscope (including on-screen scope HUD overlay with 123\302\260 Skin Tone Indicator Line, Cb/Cr chrominance scatter, and 75%/100% broadcast targets).\n  3. *Lossless High-Bitrate 4K Export in Settings*: Implement customizable export bitrates (Master 4K 100 Mbps Lossless/Near-Lossless HEVC/H.264, 4K High 60 Mbps, 1080p 25 Mbps).\n  4. *Instagram Reels Export Aspect Ratio*: Implement aspect ratio delivery modes for video rendering:\n     - `9:16` Instagram Reels / TikTok / Shorts ($1080\\times1920$ FHD or $2160\\times3840$ 4K Vertical center-crop)\n     - `16:9` Cinema / Landscape ($3840\\times2160$ 4K UHD or $1920\\times1080$)\n     - `1:1` Square ($1080\\times1080$)\n     - `2.39:1` Anamorphic Widescreen ($3840\\times1606$)\n- **Package & Environment**:\n  - Android 16 (API 36), Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, Material 3.\n  - Package: `com.example` (`applicationId: com.aistudio.colorgrader.samsunglog.lckmvd`).\n  - App Name: `ResolveStudio` (synchronized with `metadata.json` and `strings.xml`).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed Components & Verified in Current & Previous Turns**:\n  - `ColorGradeState.kt`: `CUSTOM_BEZIER` mask type, `BezierControlPoint`, `defaultBezierPoints()`, `LutCategory.FUJIFILM`, 7 Fujifilm recipe presets (`FUJI_CLASSIC_CHROME`, `FUJI_CLASSIC_NEGATIVE`, `FUJI_NOSTALGIC_NEGATIVE`, `FUJI_VELVIA`, `FUJI_PROVIA`, `FUJI_ASTIA`, `FUJI_ACROS`).\n  - `SamsungLogColorScience.kt`: Cubic Bezier math evaluation (`evaluateBezierMask`) with point-in-polygon winding & Hermite smoothstep boundary feathering; 7 Fujifilm recipe curves tuned for Samsung S24 Ultra 10-bit Log.\n  - `MaskingOverlay.kt`: Interactive Bezier spline drawing on Canvas with draggable anchor nodes, tangent handles (`handleIn`, `handleOut`), and HUD controls (+Node, -Node, Reset).\n  - `PowerWindowOverlay.kt`: Added `Bezier` selector tab, node count badge, midpoint node addition, and deletion.\n  - `LutManager.kt`: Added custom color gradients for all 7 Fujifilm recipe swatches.\n  - `RealtimeHistogramOverlay.kt`: New cinema-monitor HUD overlay over video preview with 256-bin Luma/RGB distribution, IRE graticule (0, 18% mid-gray, 50%, 75%, 100%), live shadow crush and highlight clipping telemetry, and `[RAW]` vs `[REC]` A/B toggle.\n  - `GradingStudioScreen.kt`: Fixed the header wrap bug (\"st ud\" in yellow) by replacing separate Text composables with a unified, non-wrapping `buildAnnotatedString` (`RESOLVE` in white, `STUDIO` in amber) and moving secondary actions to a 3-dots `Studio More Options` menu. Wired `showHistogramOverlay`.\n  - `VideoPlayerView.kt`: Added `histogram_overlay_toggle` icon button and rendered `RealtimeHistogramOverlay` inside the video viewport.\n  - Test suites: `compile_applet` passed; `ExampleRobolectricTest` passed (`read string from context`, `test realtime histogram calculation on bitmap`); `ExampleUnitTest` passed (33 test tasks, 0 failures).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Design Decisions\n- **Color Wheels Direct Touch**:\n  `ColorWheel.kt` currently uses `detectDragGestures` with sensitivity. Adding `detectTapGestures(onTap = { ... })` inside the color wheel Box allows direct tapping to instantly jump/bias the reticle to that touched color angle and saturation, in addition to precision drag and double-tap reset.\n- **Vectorscope Overlay**:\n  In `ScopesView.kt`, `VectorscopeCanvas` calculates Cb/Cr coordinates ($Cb = -0.168736R - 0.331264G + 0.5B$, $Cr = 0.5R - 0.418688G - 0.081312B$) and renders the $123^\\circ$ skin-tone indicator line. We can add a Scope Mode toggle (Histogram vs Vectorscope) inside `RealtimeHistogramOverlay.kt` or create `RealtimeScopeOverlay.kt` to allow users to toggle both the Histogram and Vectorscope overlays directly on the video viewport.\n- **Video Export (Lossless/High Bitrate 4K + Instagram Reels 9:16)**:\n  - In `VideoExporter.kt`:\n    - `renderGradedVideo` currently has hardcoded $12\\text{ Mbps}$ and takes `baseFrame.width` $\\times$ `baseFrame.height`.\n    - Needs an `ExportConfig` data class:\n      ```kotlin\n      enum class ExportResolution(val label: String, val width: Int, val height: Int) {\n          UHD_4K(\"4K UHD (3840x2160)\", 3840, 2160),\n          FHD_1080P(\"1080p FHD (1920x1080)\", 1920, 1080)\n      }\n      enum class ExportAspectRatio(val label: String, val aspectWidth: Int, val aspectHeight: Int, val isVertical: Boolean) {\n          CINEMA_16_9(\"16:9 Landscape (YouTube/TV)\", 16, 9, false),\n          REELS_9_16(\"9:16 Vertical (Instagram Reels/TikTok)\", 9, 16, true),\n          SQUARE_1_1(\"1:1 Square (Instagram Feed)\", 1, 1, false),\n          ANAMORPHIC_2_39(\"2.39:1 CinemaScope\", 239, 100, false)\n      }\n      enum class ExportQuality(val label: String, val bitrate: Int, val description: String) {\n          MASTER_LOSSLESS_4K(\"4K Master Lossless (100 Mbps)\", 100_000_000, \"Maximum fidelity 10-bit master\"),\n          HIGH_QUALITY(\"High Quality (60 Mbps)\", 60_000_000, \"Cinema-grade delivery\"),\n          REELS_OPTIMIZED(\"Instagram Reels Optimized (25 Mbps)\", 25_000_000, \"Ideal for social media platforms\")\n      }\n      ```\n    - When rendering 9:16 Instagram Reels, `VideoExporter` scales and center-crops the 16:9 source frame to $1080\\times1920$ or $2160\\times3840$ so the footage fills the entire vertical screen without black bars or distortion.\n  - `ExportDialog.kt` needs controls to select:\n    - **Aspect Ratio**: 16:9 Landscape vs **9:16 Instagram Reels** vs 1:1 Square\n    - **Quality/Bitrate**: 4K Master Lossless (100 Mbps) vs High Quality (60 Mbps) vs Standard\n    - **Resolution**: 4K UHD vs 1080p FHD\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes (Exhaustive Session History)\n1. `replace_file_content` failure on `ColorGradeState.kt`:\n   - *Cause*: Formatting discrepancy in target chunk.\n   - *Fix*: Used `write_to_file(Overwrite = true)` with verified complete class definition.\n2. `ColorGradeState.kt:54:5 An explicit type is required on a value parameter`:\n   - *Cause*: `val centerY = 0.5f,` lacked `: Float`.\n   - *Fix*: Changed to `val centerY: Float = 0.5f,`.\n3. `SamsungLogColorScience.kt:273:26 \'operator\' modifier is required on \'FirNamedFunctionSymbol\'`:\n   - *Cause*: Kotlin compiler inferred generic `Comparable` from `maxOf(qx / featherW, qy / featherH)`.\n   - *Fix*: Replaced with `val dist: Float = max(qx / featherW, qy / featherH)` using `kotlin.math.max` and explicit `Float` return type on `rawWeight`.\n4. JVM Unit Test failure `testRealtimeHistogramCalculation`:\n   - *Cause*: `android.graphics.Bitmap.createBitmap` is not mocked in plain JVM tests.\n   - *Fix*: Moved the bitmap test into `ExampleRobolectricTest.kt` where Robolectric mocks the Android graphics stack.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- Clean working directory; all current changes compile and pass unit tests.\n- Files open/inspected: `ColorWheel.kt`, `ScopesView.kt`, `VideoExporter.kt`, `ExportDialog.kt`, `GradingViewModel.kt`, `GradingStudioScreen.kt`.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps (Actionable Priority Order)\n1. **Update `app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/ColorWheel.kt`**:\n   - In `Box.pointerInput`, add `onTap` to `detectTapGestures` to allow direct touch-to-color positioning in addition to drag.\n   - Ensure Lift, Gamma, and Gain wheels provide immediate tactile response with numeric RGB offset badges and reset capabilities.\n2. **Enhance Vectorscope / Scope Overlay**:\n   - Update `RealtimeHistogramOverlay.kt` (or create `RealtimeScopeOverlay.kt` / extend scope overlay) to support a **VECTORSCOPE** tab right on the video overlay.\n   - Display polar grid, 75%/100% broadcast targets, and the 123\302\260 skin tone reference line directly in the on-screen overlay HUD.\n3. **Update `app/src/main/java/com/example/video/VideoExporter.kt`**:\n   - Define `ExportAspectRatio` (`CINEMA_16_9`, `REELS_9_16`, `SQUARE_1_1`, `ANAMORPHIC_2_39`), `ExportResolution` (`UHD_4K`, `FHD_1080P`), and `ExportQuality` (`MASTER_LOSSLESS_4K` at 100 Mbps, `HIGH_QUALITY` at 60 Mbps, `REELS_OPTIMIZED` at 25 Mbps).\n   - In `renderGradedVideo`, calculate target dimensions based on chosen aspect ratio (e.g. $1080\\times1920$ or $2160\\times3840$ for Instagram Reels), perform center-crop bitmap scaling, and configure `MediaFormat` with selected high bitrate.\n4. **Update `app/src/main/java/com/example/ui/components/ExportDialog.kt`**:\n   - Add Aspect Ratio selector chips (`16:9 Cinema`, `9:16 Instagram Reels`, `1:1 Square`).\n   - Add Quality/Bitrate selector chips (`4K Lossless 100M`, `4K High 60M`, `Reels 25M`).\n   - Pass selected `ExportConfig` to `onExportVideo(config)`.\n5. **Update `GradingViewModel.kt` & `GradingStudioScreen.kt`**:\n   - Wire the export configuration from `ExportDialog` into `viewModel.exportVideo(config)`.\n6. **Add Unit Tests in `app/src/test/java/com/example/ExampleUnitTest.kt`**:\n   - Test Instagram Reels 9:16 dimension calculations ($1080\\times1920$, $2160\\times3840$).\n   - Test bitrate parameters (100 Mbps, 60 Mbps, 25 Mbps).\n7. **Verification**:\n   - Run `compile_applet`.\n   - Run `gradle :app:testDebugUnitTest`.\n   - Run `gradle :app:assembleDebug`.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Keep `name` in `metadata.json` and `res/values/strings.xml` synced to `\"ResolveStudio\"`.\n- Do not remove `MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API` from `metadata.json`.\n- Do not create or edit `local.properties`.\n- Use Jetpack Compose and Material 3 exclusively.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 221
    included_step_index_end: 508
