  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Gesture Handling**\n\nI\'ve been focusing on the gesture handling within the `ColorWheel.kt` file, specifically lines 187-209. The goal is to make it more intuitive. I\'ve been experimenting with the `detectTapGestures` implementation. It seems like I need to refine the way the gestures are recognized. I\'m considering adding additional gesture support.\n\n\n**Implementing Tap Gestures**\n\nI\'ve added `onTap` to `detectTapGestures` now. It addresses the issue of direct color selection. Touching the color wheel anywhere instantly sets the reticle to that color. I\'m calculating the tap offset relative to the Box size and normalizing it. I have formulas for dx, dy to determine the target color on the wheel. This involves calculating the center of the color wheel and using the radius, `R`, to map tap coordinates to hue and saturation values.\n\n\n"
