    thinking: "**Visualize the Placement**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `GradingStudioScreen.kt` file. It\'s becoming clear that when `showScopes` is active, the `ScopesView` with the `gradedBitmap` needs to be displayed. I\'m considering the ideal location for this: in portrait mode, it should sit between the `VideoPlayerView` and the `StudioDockContainer`, possibly expandable. In landscape, it should be above or beside the `StudioDockContainer`.\n\n\n**Integrate Scopes Overlay**\n\nI\'m now integrating the vectorscope directly into the `VideoPlayerView`. My plan is to include a toggle within the `RealtimeHistogramOverlay` to switch between the histogram and the new vectorscope. The vectorscope overlay will feature a polar graticule, a skin tone indicator, color target boxes, and real-time chroma scatter. This should integrate seamlessly with the full Broadcast Scopes dock card when the `showScopes` button is tapped.\n\n\n"
