  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Request**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the core of the user\'s request. It\'s about implementing interactive color wheels (Lift, Gamma, Gain) with touch-based adjustments, ensuring precise color grading. Additionally, I need to incorporate a vectorscope. I\'m focusing on these elements to ensure they\'re central to the design.\n\n\n**Adding Export Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now integrating lossless high bitrate 4k export into settings and implementing the export ratio feature for Instagram Reels. I\'m focusing on the architectural design for this, aiming to ensure intuitive user control and seamless integration with the existing export workflow. This also needs to work with the touch-based features for color grading, and vectorscope functionality.\n\n\n**Implementing Color Offsets**\n\nI\'m now integrating primary color channel offset badges (R, G, B) into the color grading interface, mirroring DaVinci Resolve\'s functionality. This includes displaying R, G, B offset values for Lift, Gamma, and Gain using `SamsungLogColorScience.wheelToRgbShift()`. I\'m designing small pills with color-coded text (red, green, blue) to represent the offsets and displaying related info such as hue, saturation and the Master Luminance slider. Furthermore, I\'ve added a double-tap-to-reset feature for hue & saturation, and touch-drag left/right functionality for the master luminance jog wheel.\n\n\n**Defining Scope Views**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing scope views within `GradingStudioScreen.kt`. The aim is to provide users with broadcast-fidelity Waveform Parade, Vectorscope, and Histogram displays. I\'m exploring telemetry readouts for skin-tone alignment, peak saturation, and legal gamut checks, as well as considering toggle buttons for switching between histogram/vectorscope and raw/rec views. I\'ve also identified specific color targets for the chroma space analysis.\n\n\n**Defining Export Parameters**\n\nI\'m now defining the export parameters. I\'ve established aspect ratios like 16:9 and 9:16, alongside bitrates for different quality levels, including a lossless 4K option. These parameters will ensure users have fine-grained control over their export settings. I\'m focusing on user-friendly labels and descriptions for each preset.\n\n\n**Defining Export Config**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining a `VideoExportConfig` data class. This includes resolution, aspect ratio, quality (with a lossless 4K option), frame rate, and duration. For Instagram Reels, I\'m specifically setting vertical 9:16 aspect ratios for various resolutions, ensuring compatibility. I\'m focusing on balancing file size and export quality for quick sharing, particularly for the Reels aspect ratio.\n\n\n**Calculating Frame Transformations**\n\nI\'m now detailing the calculations for transforming source frames to the 9:16 Instagram Reels format, focusing on proper center-cropping. I\'m calculating the scale factor, scaled dimensions, and offsets to ensure full frame fill without black bars, perfectly centered on subject action. I\'m also ensuring the correct configuration of `MediaFormat` parameters.\n\n\n\n"
