    thinking: "**Analyzing Code Context**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `GradingStudioScreen.kt`, specifically line 541 where `showScopes` dictates the display of `ScopesView`. I\'m examining how the `previewBitmap` is handled within this conditional block. My aim is to understand the logic flow and dependencies in this area.\n\n\n**Examining `GradedBitmap` Usage**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on how `gradedBitmap` is utilized in both portrait and landscape orientations within `GradingStudioScreen.kt`. Specifically, I see its usage in both `ScopesView` and directly rendered. I am observing the differences in the modifiers applied to `gradedBitmap` based on the screen orientation. This helps reveal where design decisions have influenced `gradedBitmap` handling.\n\n\n**Defining Export Features**\n\nI\'m now outlining key functionalities within `VideoExporter.kt`. I\'m structuring `ExportResolution` with UHD_4K and FHD_1080P options, and am defining `ExportAspectRatio` with REELS_9_16. This is the initial setup to manage 4K exports and Instagram Reels aspect ratios.\n\n\n**Structuring Export Configuration**\n\nI\'m now detailing `ExportAspectRatio`, expanding beyond Reels with Cinema, Square, and Anamorphic options, complete with display names, aspect ratios, and boolean flags. Subsequently, I\'ve outlined `ExportBitrateQuality`, which includes options from lossless 4K to standard quality settings with accompanying descriptions. I have also begun defining the `VideoExportConfig` data class to house these options.\n\n\n**Determining Pixel Dimensions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `getTargetDimensions` function. This calculates target width and height based on the defined `ExportResolution` and `ExportAspectRatio`. I\'m handling the various aspect ratios and resolutions, ensuring that the dimensions are even numbers as required by video codecs.\n\n\n**Implementing Center-Crop Logic**\n\nI\'ve just focused on rendering a graded frame onto the target surface using a center-crop approach. The `baseFrame`, sourced from an example like $3840 \\times 2160$, is graded to produce `gradedFrame`. I am now working on hardware canvas of size $W_t \\times H_t$, where I have defined and implemented the `scale`, `scaledW`, `scaledH`, `dx`, `dy`, `srcRect`, and `dstRect`, ensuring an elegant center-crop result for the final output.\n\n\n**Refining Center-Crop Strategy**\n\nI\'m verifying the center-crop logic within the codec format and confirming its impact on the output. Currently, for a REELS_9_16 aspect ratio, horizontal 16:9 footage should be scaled up to fill the vertical frame without distortion. I\'m also ensuring the CINEMA_16_9 aspect ratio fits precisely.\n\nI\'m exploring the `MediaFormat` configuration for the video codec, examining bitrate settings, frame rates, and the critical `COLOR_FormatSurface`. I\'m verifying 100 Mbps achieves lossless cinema bitrate. I am planning to review and fully rewrite VideoExporter.kt.\n\n\n"
