  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding Test Cases**\n\nI\'m currently working on adding new test cases to `ExampleUnitTest.kt`. I\'m focusing on validating video export dimensions, specifically for Instagram Reels. I\'ve got a couple of 9:16 and 16:9 aspect ratios in mind, including 4K UHD and 1080p FHD resolutions. There\'s also a square 1:1 aspect ratio that needs to be handled.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_234595"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Add unit tests for Instagram Reels 9:16 export, 4K lossless 100 Mbps bitrate, and primary wheel RGB shift\",\"EndLine\":445,\"Instruction\":\"Append new tests for Reels export dimensions, bitrates, and primary wheels RGB shift\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"        assertTrue(\\\"Velvia red saturation punch\\\", (vr - vb) > (asr - asb))\\n    }\\n\\n    @Test\\n    fun testInstagramReelsExportDimensions() {\\n        val reels4k = com.example.video.VideoExportConfig(\\n            resolution = com.example.video.ExportResolution.UHD_4K,\\n            aspectRatio = com.example.video.ExportAspectRatio.REELS_9_16\\n        )\\n        val (w4k, h4k) = reels4k.getTargetDimensions()\\n        assertEquals(2160, w4k)\\n        assertEquals(3840, h4k)\\n\\n        val reelsFhd = com.example.video.VideoExportConfig(\\n            resolution = com.example.video.ExportResolution.FHD_1080P,\\n            aspectRatio = com.example.video.ExportAspectRatio.REELS_9_16\\n        )\\n        val (wFhd, hFhd) = reelsFhd.getTargetDimensions()\\n        assertEquals(1080, wFhd)\\n        assertEquals(1920, hFhd)\\n\\n        val cinema4k = com.example.video.VideoExportConfig(\\n            resolution = com.example.video.ExportResolution.UHD_4K,\\n            aspectRatio = com.example.video.ExportAspectRatio.CINEMA_16_9\\n        )\\n        val (cw, ch) = cinema4k.getTargetDimensions()\\n        assertEquals(3840, cw)\\n        assertEquals(2160, ch)\\n\\n        val square = com.example.video.VideoExportConfig(\\n            resolution = com.example.video.ExportResolution.FHD_1080P,\\n            aspectRatio = com.example.video.ExportAspectRatio.SQUARE_1_1\\n        )\\n        val (sw, sh) = square.getTargetDimensions()\\n        assertEquals(1080, sw)\\n        assertEquals(1080, sh)\\n    }\\n\\n    @Test\\n    fun testExportQualityBitrates() {\\n        val master = com.example.video.ExportBitrateQuality.LOSSLESS_MASTER_4K\\n        assertEquals(100_000_000, master.bitrateBps)\\n        assertTrue(master.isLosslessMaster)\\n\\n        val highCinema = com.example.video.ExportBitrateQuality.HIGH_QUALITY_60M\\n        assertEquals(60_000_000, highCinema.bitrateBps)\\n\\n        val reelsOptimized = com.example.video.ExportBitrateQuality.REELS_OPTIMIZED_25M\\n        assertEquals(25_000_000, reelsOptimized.bitrateBps)\\n\\n        val standard = com.example.video.ExportBitrateQuality.BALANCED_12M\\n        assertEquals(12_000_000, standard.bitrateBps)\\n    }\\n\\n    @Test\\n    fun testPrimaryColorWheelRgbShift() {\\n        // Center position (0, 0) gives neutral zero offset\\n        val (r0, g0, b0) = SamsungLogColorScience.wheelToRgbShift(0f, 0f)\\n        assertEquals(0f, r0, 0.001f)\\n        assertEquals(0f, g0, 0.001f)\\n        assertEquals(0f, b0, 0.001f)\\n\\n        // Pure top (y=1) biases green\\n        val (rg, gg, bg) = SamsungLogColorScience.wheelToRgbShift(0f, 1f)\\n        assertEquals(1f, gg, 0.001f)\\n        assertEquals(-0.5f, rg, 0.001f)\\n        assertEquals(-0.5f, bg, 0.001f)\\n\\n        // Pure right (x=1) biases red over blue\\n        val (rr, gr, br) = SamsungLogColorScience.wheelToRgbShift(1f, 0f)\\n        assertTrue(rr > 0f)\\n        assertTrue(br < 0f)\\n        assertEquals(0f, gr, 0.001f)\\n    }\\n}\",\"StartLine\":442,\"TargetContent\":\"        assertTrue(\\\"Velvia red saturation punch\\\", (vr - vb) > (asr - asb))\\n    }\\n}\",\"TargetFile\":\"/app/src/test/java/com/example/ExampleUnitTest.kt\",\"toolAction\":\"Adding export & wheels unit tests\",\"toolSummary\":\"Add tests for Reels 9:16, 100Mbps 4K, and color wheels in ExampleUnitTest.kt\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\247\b\n\244\b\001i\024}\023D;DZ\350}\271\216\001@`Z\234&\352dnT\337X\353\244\177Pxy\027\210\365\017yWf\005Yg\325c\227\270q\230`\360\213bs\223\036\360\n\366\274\304\372\232f\356\310\023A\277qI\316P`=\351\003<\"\351\2772\266!P\252\372\2036\300\271D\256#\tV\312\000O\340\200\030\226K0\001\257\345\370O\246\320\223M\256\'\265\254\331\r\236\245%\326\257\216\315\372\352\207\226\323\330M\026\362\347w!\235n\311L\002(R?\377\270\260\346\r`w|DP\326Szf\\\313g\306\253,\023\004\376\351\367x\313\247NO\302\222\022q\230\202\256\333\3109\031\267TN\373<\033\365\235\001\373;\361@\017\035eU\254\310\236\266\266\357\340\250\035\275+\351\372\320\333}\212\363#^\257}\306C^\312\216\232\270\332o\232\247\246j\370?\201ak\222\257\031\266\305\023ny\362E\233\2537X\337\v@\2003\034\233\220\311\375\001e\312\240\"\340p\236#\021\354:\"\322\340\311\306\271\275;\004\006\374\325w\221/3\224[\252F\004\325l,G\320\315\223P\227\364\245g*\243\235tc\267,\317\215\312\341@\3014\352\255>72\005\314/\254\212\373[\310H\tI\211\213<\204sV\207\270\3468~?D\003Es\223\212  \016\350Q=\262\026y\306\210\316\310\003u\002\027D\357\221\272\270\263~\311\207\302\337{\306\236\266\333\276A0\215pj\235\017\240\355p\036\372\222V0\3660b\324\346\370\215p7\317\272\004\027DQ\f\337\205\311\350B\376\017o\341\302}\034\000@\245\vo\322U\345\3618z\024\251OVk\214N_F\316GS\213s\233\2061\276\324\264\\\223\334zA,\201\233\033\031<{\036\201\324d\020G\233\332%\366N\333\360\304\255{\f\363\214\226\320$B\275b\225\345eH\215MAK\312\242U\200j\312l\261\320X;\241\212o\035{Q\235:\031\321\217r\322\'\332\020\030\260\021\306~\314\255\315\343\v\233A\345<\374M\251-\234\323\274w+;\256Y\rW\234\347{5\310m\316\360j\r\335\372\347\371\245\255\267\034\241\352\334#\303c\016\n\370\247\332|\334\237_Y\212!\377\336\243\352\\\bd\0172\2125\300(\021A\2702L1f\221\3633f\177>\035\214N\"/\271<Gr\352\266W\336\276\260\347\301\276\006\036\023\3028\327#XEe\203\222\rI3#\267?\001\373\204\243\036\004\375\243\247%9\333g\361\257$\371q\324\340P\246d\305#i%\265\212\27